Calculations for Loading Dose Based on Individual''s In Vivo Recovery (IVR)

  Prior to surgery: Measure plasma VWF:RCo at baseline. Infuse 60 international units VWF:RCo/kg IV at time Measure plasma VWF:RCo 30 min-
  utes later. Calculate the in vivo recovery (IVR) as follows 4 :
   ●   IVR = (Plasma VWF:RCo 30 minutes - Plasma VWF:RCo baseline) divided by 60 international units/kg
   ●   Loading dose: ((Plasma VWF:RCotarget peak - Plasma VWF:RCo baseline) X weight (kg)) divided by IVR (patient specific)
   ●   * If the calculated IVR exceeds 5, use the value 5 to calculate the recommended loading dose to avoid under-dosing.
