  During clinical trials, no adverse reactions or inhibitors to Factor VIII were reported in patients with hemophilia A. In patients with von Willebrand
  disease, the most commonly reported adverse effects (greater than 1%) were pruritus, headache, back pain, paresthesia, respiratory distress, fa-
  cial edema, pain, rash, and chills Humate-P®
  The most commonly reported adverse reactions for treatment of bleeding episodes in von Willebrand disease (VWD) were allergic-anaphylactic
  reactions. Additional adverse reactions included chills, phlebitis, vasodilation, paresthesia, pruritus, rash, and urticaria. For prevention of exces-
  sive bleeding during and after surgery in VWD patients, the most commonly reported hemorrhagic adverse reactions were wound/injection site
  bleeding and epistaxis 2

  Wilate®
  In clinical trials of patients with VWD, the most commonly reported adverse reactions were hypersensitivity reaction (1.9%), urticaria (1.3%), and
  dizziness (1.3%). In clinical trials of patients with hemophilia A, the most commonly reported adverse reaction was pyrexia (1.5%) Monitoring
