  age (n=17), 87+/-3.31 mL/kg/hr in individuals 12 to less than 18 years of age (n=8) and 27+/-0.84 mL/kg/hr in adults (n=18). Because children
  younger than 12 years have a higher mean clearance (based on body weight), a shorter mean half-life, and lower incremental recovery of factor
