   Preparation

   Use only the supplied diluent to reconstitute; the sterile diluent is provided in either a vial or
   prefilled syringe Vial: To reconstitute the vaccine, withdraw the entire volume of the supplied sterile diluent
   from the vial and slowly inject into the lyophilized vaccine vial; gently agitate to dissolve com-
   pletely; discard if the lyophilized vaccine cannot be dissolved Prefilled syringe: Attach a needle to the prefilled syringe; reconstitute the vaccine by slowly
   injecting the entire volume of sterile diluent contained in the prefilled syringe into the
   lyophilized vaccine vial; gently agitate to dissolve completely; discard if the lyophilized vaccine
   cannot be dissolved Reconstituted vaccine is a clear, colorless to pale yellow liquid; do not use the reconstituted
   vaccine if particulates are present or if it appears discolored Do not combine with any other vaccine through reconstitution or mixing Following reconstitution, use the vaccine immediately; discard if not used within 30 minutes of
   reconstitution. Do not freeze reconstituted vaccine', 'Common:
   • Varicella-like generalized rash, 8% to 5% after dose 1 with peak occurrence 5 to 26 days
