   • Other common reactions: Injection-site reactions (ie, soreness, erythema, swelling), 3% to 5%; fever 102°F (38.9°C) or greater in patients 1 to 12 years, 7%; .fever 100°F (37.8°C) or
   greater in patients 13 years or older, 5% to 2% 4

   Herpes zoster infection: 8 cases have been reported in children during follow-up in clinical
   trials, with a calculated incidence of at least 8 cases per 100,000 person-years. This appears
   to be similar to the rate in healthy children who had wild-type varicella. One case has been re-
   ported in adolescents and adults, with a calculated incidence of at least 5 cases per 100,000
   person-years. All 9 cases were mild and without sequelae 4

