   glutamate synthase; ASS = argininosuccinic acid synthetase; ASL = argininosuccinic acid lyase', 'Adjunctive treatment of acute hyperammonemia in infants and children with urea cycle disor-
   ders. Sodium phenylacetate/sodium benzoate should be used concomitantly with arginine hy-
   drochloride. Hemodialysis is the primary treatment of acute hyperammonemia during the
   early management period 7 ,3 ,4 ,5 ,6 . Caloric supplementation, dietary protein restriction, and
   other ammonia lowering therapies should also be considered during acute hyperammonemic
   episodes Administration
   Must be administered through a central line. For loading and maintenance doses, dilute
   sodium phenylacetate/sodium benzoate and arginine in 25 to 35 mL/kg of D10W prior to ad-
   ministration. Infuse the loading dose over 90 to 120 minutes 7 ,', 'The most common adverse effects include vomiting (9%), hyperglycemia (7%), and hy-
   pokalemia (7%). Vomiting and lethargy can occur with higher than recommended doses.
   Potentially life-threatening toxicity can occur with doses greater than 750 mg/kg/day.
   Extravasation may lead to tissue necrosis; administration through central line required 7 ,5 .

