   weight in kg)/100 20 kg or greater: dose (in vials) = (serum digoxin concentration in ng/mL x weight in kg)/100 1/5
Dosage calculations are based on a steady-state volume of distribution of approximately 5
   L/kg for digoxin to convert serum digoxin concentration to the amount of digoxin in the body.
   These volumes are population averages and vary widely among individuals. Many patients
