   (4 to 8 mg/mL) 4 ,5 .

   Solution Preparation Calculations
   To calculate the AMOUNT of drug needed per defined final fluid volume:
   Desired final concentration (mg/mL) x defined final fluid volume (mL) = AMOUNT of drug to
   add to final infusion solution (mg).
   To calculate the VOLUME of drug needed per defined final fluid volume:

*AMOUNT of drug to add (mg) ÷ drug (vial) concentration (mg/mL) = VOLUME of drug to add
   (mL)
   Example (for Lidocaine): Mix 50 mL of 2400 mcg/mL solution using lidocaine concentration of
   20 mg/mL.
   2400 mcg/mL = 4 mg/mL 4 mg/mL × 50 mL = 120 mg lidocaine
   *120 mg ÷ 20 mg/mL = 6 mL of lidocaine
   Add 6 mL of lidocaine (20 mg/mL) to 44 mL of compatible solution (eg, D5W) to yield 50 mL of
   infusion solution with a concentration of 2400 mcg/mL.
   Maximum concentration is 8000 mcg/mL.

