   12 years or older and 35 kg or greater
   Optional oral lead-in dosing ( to assess the tolerability): Cabotegravir 30 mg orally in com-
   bination with rilpivirine 25 mg orally once daily with a meal for approximately 1 month (at least
   28 days) 1
   Monthly Dosing Schedule
   Initiation: Cabotegravir 600 mg IM and rilpivirine 900 mg IM as separate gluteal injections
   during the same visit; if using optional oral lead-in dosing, initiate injection on last day of oral
   lead-in therapy Maintenance: Cabotegravir 400 mg IM and rilpivirine 600 mg IM as separate gluteal injections
   every month; begin continuation injections 1 month after initiation injections; maintenance in-
   jections may be administered up to 7 days before or after the date the patient is scheduled to
   receive monthly injections Planned missed injection: If a patient plans to miss a scheduled injection visit by more than 7
   days, administer daily oral therapy for up to 2 months to replace missed injection visits.
   Administer the first dose of oral therapy approximately 1 month after the last dose and con-
   tinue until the day injection dose is restarted. The oral replacement dosage is cabotegravir 30
   mg orally in combination with rilpivirine 25 mg orally once daily with a meal Unplanned missed injection: If scheduled injections are missed or delayed more than 7 days
   and oral therapy has not been taken in the interim, clinically reassess the patient to determine

if resumption of injection dosing remains appropriate. See the following table for appropriate
   dosing based on time since last injection 1 :

