   HIV Infected Patients: Liposomal amphotericin B is a recommended first-line agent for the
   following infections in HIV infected patients: 11,10,12
   ●   Coccidioidomycosis, including severe illness with respiratory compromise due to diffuse
       pulmonary or disseminated non-meningeal infection, fluconazole-refractory meningeal
       infection
   ●   Cryptococcosis, including CNS disease, disseminated disease (CNS not involved), and severe
       pulmonary disease
   ●   Histoplasmosis, including moderately severe to severe disseminated disease and CNS
       infection

   Meningitis/Ventriculitis, Hospital Acquired: Based on in vitro susceptibility testing, lipid for-
   mulation amphotericin B, often in combination with 5-flucytosine, is the preferred treatment
   option for healthcare associated meningitis and ventriculitis caused by Candida species.
   Therapy may be changed to fluconazole if the isolated species is susceptible and patient shows
   clinical signs of improvement. Lipid formulation amphotericin B is also a suitable alternative
   therapy for infections caused by Aspergillus species Pediatric FDA-Approved Indications

   Empirical therapy for presumed fungal infection in febrile, neutropenic patients Treatment of Cryptococcal meningitis in HIV-infected patients 18,3 .

   Treatment of patients with Aspergillus species, Candida species and/or Cryptococcus species
   infections refractory to amphotericin B deoxycholate, or in patients where renal impairment or
   unacceptable toxicity precludes the use of amphotericin B deoxycholate Treatment of visceral leishmaniasis 3 , 19 , Administration

