(122, 'Albuterol/Ipratropium', 'respiratory', TRUE, FALSE, FALSE, 100, 'Acute Asthma Exacerbation-Albuterol and Ipratropium Combination Product
   Metered-dose inhaler

   Less than 12 years of age: Inhale 4 to 8 puffs every 20 minutes as needed for up to 3 hours 12 years or older: Inhale 8 puffs every 20 minutes as needed for up to 3 hours Solution for inhalation

   Less than 12 years of age: 5 to 3 mL by nebulizer every 20 minutes for 3 doses then give as
   needed for up to 3 hours 12 years or older: 3 mL by nebulizer every 20 minutes for 3 doses then give as ne', 'Not FDA approved in children 2 ,3 ,5 .

Administration
   Inhalation spray:
   Combivent® Respimat®: Insert drug cartridge into the inhaler and prime the inhaler prior to
   first use. To prime, hold the inhaler upright with the orange cap closed, then turn the clear
   base in the direction of the white arrows on the label until it clicks (half a turn). Flip off the or-
   ange cap so it is fully open. For first time use and if inhaler has not been used for more than 21
   days, point the inha', 'Common adverse events include headache, dyspnea, nasopharyngitis, and cough. Dry mouth
   and taste perversion (bitter taste) have also been reported frequently with inhalation aerosol
   2 ,3 ,5
             .

   Monitoring
   Assess degree of bronchospasm. Monitor respiratory rate, heart rate, and blood pressure.
   Measure pulmonary function tests.', '', 'Pharmacology
   The combination of albuterol and ipratropium produces bronchodilation through two distinct
   mechanisms and greater bronchodilation than either drug individually Albuterol is a specific β2-adrenergic agonist. Stimulates production of intracellular cyclic AMP,
   enhancing the binding of intracellular calcium to the cell membrane and endoplasmic reticu-
   lum, resulting in bronchodilation. Mean onset of action for inhalation in patients 4 to 11 years
   of age is approximately 8', 'Acute Asthma Exacerbation-Albuterol and Ipratropium Combination Product
   Metered-dose inhaler

   Less than 12 years of age: Inhale 4 to 8 puffs every 20 minutes as needed for up to 3 hours 12 years or older: Inhale 8 puffs every 20 minutes as needed for up to 3 hours Solution for inhalation

   Less than 12 years of age: 5 to 3 mL by nebulizer every 20 minutes for 3 doses then give as
   needed for up to 3 hours 12 years or older: 3 mL by nebulizer every 20 minutes for 3 doses then give as needed for up
   to 3 hours', 'Not FDA approved in children 2 ,3 ,5 .

Administration
   Inhalation spray:
   Combivent® Respimat®: Insert drug cartridge into the inhaler and prime the inhaler prior to
   first use. To prime, hold the inhaler upright with the orange cap closed, then turn the clear
   base in the direction of the white arrows on the label until it clicks (half a turn). Flip off the or-
   ange cap so it is fully open. For first time use and if inhaler has not been used for more than 21
   days, point the inhaler toward the ground, press the dose release button, then close the or-
   ange cap. Once an aerosol cloud is visible, then actuate 3 more times. If the inhaler has not
   been used for more than 3 days, then actuate the inhaler once. Do not cover the air vents
   when administering the inhaler. Avoid contact with the eyes Metered-dose inhaler:
   Combivent®: Test spray the metered dose inhaler (MDI) 3 times before first use or when MDI
   has not been used for greater than 24 hours. Shake the canister for a minimum of 10 seconds
   before use. Discard when the labeled number of sprays has been used. Avoid contact with the
   eyes Use a spacer or a valve holding chamber in younger patients (less than 5 years of age)
   or patients with poor inhaler technique. A mask should be added for children less than 4 years
   of age Solution for inhalation: Administer via jet nebulizer connected to an air compressor with an
   adequate air flow with a mouthpiece connection A tight-fitting face mask should be used in
   patients who cannot use a mouthpiece Avoid contact with the eyes', 'Common adverse events include headache, dyspnea, nasopharyngitis, and cough. Dry mouth
   and taste perversion (bitter taste) have also been reported frequently with inhalation aerosol
   2 ,3 ,5
             .

   Monitoring
   Assess degree of bronchospasm. Monitor respiratory rate, heart rate, and blood pressure.
   Measure pulmonary function tests.', '', 'Pharmacology
   The combination of albuterol and ipratropium produces bronchodilation through two distinct
   mechanisms and greater bronchodilation than either drug individually Albuterol is a specific β2-adrenergic agonist. Stimulates production of intracellular cyclic AMP,
   enhancing the binding of intracellular calcium to the cell membrane and endoplasmic reticu-
   lum, resulting in bronchodilation. Mean onset of action for inhalation in patients 4 to 11 years
   of age is approximately 8 minutes and peak bronchodilation occurs at approximately 90 min-
   utes. Duration is 2 to 6 hours for inhalation route. Primarily eliminated through renal excretion
   (80% to 100%). Half-life in adults is approximately 5 to 6 hours for the inhalation
   aerosol/solution 13 , Ipratropium bromide is a quaternary ammonium derivative of atropine. It produces primarily
   large airway bronchodilation by antagonizing the action of acetylcholine at its receptor site. It
   is relatively bronchospecific when administered by inhalation because of limited absorption
   through lung tissue. Peak effect occurs 1 to 2 hours after administration. Duration of effect is 4
   to 6 hours in children. Half-life is approximately 2 hours after inhalation administration'),
