  Ampicillin/sulbactam is not recommended for community-acquired intra-abdominal infections because of the high rates of
  resistance of Escherichia coli Initial: 200 mg/kg/day ampicillin component IV divided every 6 hours 7 ; maximum 2000 mg ampicillin
  component/dose (3 g/dose ampicillin/sulbactam) Osteomyelitis, acute hematogenous: 100 to 200 mg/kg/day ampicillin component IV divided every 6 hours 9 ; maxi-
  mum 2000 mg ampicillin component/dose (3 g/dose ampicillin/sulbactam) Duration of therapy: Total duration of oral plus IV therapy is 4 to 6 weeks Pelvic inflammatory disease

  Adolescents: 2 g/dose ampicillin component (3 g/dose ampicillin/sulbactam/dose) IV every 6 hours plus doxycycline
  100 mg orally or IV every 12 hours Sinusitis, acute bacterial: 50 to 100 mg/kg/dose of ampicillin component (75 to 150 mg/kg/dose ampicillin plus sul-
  bactam component) IV every 6 hours (maximum 2000 mg ampicillin component/dose (3 g/dose
  ampicillin/sulbactam)) Duration of therapy: Switch to an oral antibiotic (amoxicillin-clavulanate) when clinically appropriate. Total duration
  of oral plus IV therapy is 10 to 14 days Skin and soft tissue infection
  1 year or older

  Less than 40 kg: 50 mg/kg/dose ampicillin component IV every 6 hours; maximum 2000 mg ampicillin
  component/dose (3 g/dose ampicillin/sulbactam) 40 kg or more: 1 to 2 g/dose ampicillin component (1.5 to 3 g/dose ampicillin plus sulbactam) IV every 6 hours; maxi-
