  Surgical prophylaxis The American Society of Health-System Pharmacists (ASHP) in collaboration with the Infectious
  Disease Society of America, the Surgical Infection Society, and the Society for Healthcare Epidemiology of America have
  developed guidelines for the use of antimicrobial agents for the prevention of surgical-site infections. To access the
  guideline, copy and paste this URL in your browser:  and search for Clinical Practice Guidelines for
  Antimicrobial Prophylaxis in Surgery Cefazolin is the drug of choice for antimicrobial prophylaxis for most procedures based on its wide use and proven ef-
  ficacy, spectrum of activity covering organisms commonly encountered in the surgical setting, favorable safety profile,
  and low cost 12

