   •30 kg to less than 40 kg: Atovaquone 750 mg/proguanil 300 mg (3 adult tablets) orally once
   daily for 3 days 3
   •40 kg or more: Atovaquone 1000 mg/proguanil 400 mg (4 adult tablets) orally once daily for 3
   days 3
   Concomitant medication (antirelapse treatment for P. vivax and P. ovale infections):
   Primaquine sulfate 5 mg/kg base (0.8 mg/kg salt) orally once daily for 14 days 3

   Dose adjustments
   Renal impairment

   •Mild to moderate impairment (CrCl 30 to 80 mL/min): No adjustment necessary 1
   •Severe impairment (CrCl less than 30 mL/min): Use for malaria prophylaxis is contraindi-
   cated; for malaria treatment, use with caution and only if the benefits outweigh the potential
   risks associated with increased drug exposure 1

   Hepatic impairment

   •Mild to moderate impairment: No adjustment necessary 1

   •Severe impairment: No formal studies conducted; no specific recommendations are avail-
   able 1', 'Malaria: Atovaquone/proguanil is indicated for chemoprophylaxis and treatment of malaria.
   The CDC recommends the use of atovaquone/proguanil for the treatment of malaria in the fol-
