   tant or has unknown resistance • Uncomplicated malaria infections caused by P. vivax or P. ovale, sensitive OR resistant to
   chloroquine; antirelapse therapy is required • Severe malaria infections: If IV artesunate is unavailable, may use oral therapy until arte-
   sunate is obtained. Once parasite load is 1% or less, may switch to oral therapy to complete

