   Hepatitis C with HIV Co-infection: Glecaprevir/pibrentasvir are recommended as a first-line
   treatment for hepatitis C for all genotypes in adolescent patients with HIV infection 9/15
Pediatric FDA-Approved Uses
   Indicated for the treatment of pediatric patients 3 years or older with chronic hepatitis C virus
   (HCV) genotype 1, 2, 3, 4, 5, or 6 infection without cirrhosis or with compensated cirrhosis
   (Child-Pugh A) and in patients with HCV genotype 1 infection who previously have been treated
   with a regimen containing a HCV NS5A inhibitor or an NS3/4A protease inhibitor, but not both Administration
   • Administer with food • Administer at the same time each day Pellets
   • Sprinkle the total daily dose on a small amount of soft and low-water content food that sticks
   to a spoon and can be swallowed without chewing (eg, peanut butter, chocolate hazelnut
   spread, cream cheese, thick jam, or Greek yogurt) • Swallow the entire mixture of food and pellets within 15 minutes of preparation, without
   crushing or chewing • Avoid administering with liquids or foods that can drip or slide off a spoon. They may quickly
   dissolve the drug and make it less effective • Missed Dose: If a dose is missed, tell the patient to take a missed dose as soon as possible if
