   Administration
   Administration

   Administer IM in the anterolateral thigh (preferred in infants and young children) or deltoid
   (older children; preferred in adolescents 2 , The vaccine may be administered subcutaneously in patients at risk for hemorrhage following
   IM injection, but the immune response may be lower 2 ,3 ,5 .
   A 22- to 25-gauge needle should be used. The appropriate needle length is 7/8” to 1” for in-
   fants, 7/8” to 1¼” for toddlers, older children, and adolescents Preparation

   Use vaccines as supplied; do not dilute. Shake well before withdrawal and use. 6 ,', 'Fever, fatigue, and injection site soreness are common. Rare anaphylactic reactions (ie, hives,
