   Preparation

   • Determine the number of vials to be reconstituted based on the calculated dose • Remove vials from refrigeration and set aside for approximately 20 to 30 minutes to allow
   vials to reach room temperature • Reconstitute each vial with Sterile Water for Injection (1.1 mL for 4 mg vial and 1 mL for 20
   mg vial) by directing the diluent flow to the inside wall of the vial to avoid foaming 5/9
• Gently roll and tilt vial(s) to reconstitute and avoid foaming. Each reconstituted vial will yield a
   4-mg/mL clear, colorless solution • Withdraw the required volume from the vial(s) and dilute the solution with NS in a syringe or
   infusion bag depending on the volume of infusion. Final concentration is 1 mg/mL. See fol-
