Peginterferon alfa-2a induces innate antiviral immune response by stimulating the production
4548 ng x hour/mL) Inhibits CYP1A2 (increases theophylline, methadone levels)', 'Pharmacology
   Peginterferon alfa-2a induces innate antiviral immune response by stimulating the production
   of effector proteins. In a pharmacokinetic study (n=14, age=2 to 8 years), steady state serum
   levels were observed after approximately 12 weeks of once weekly dosing (5 to 8 weeks for
   adults). Pediatric clearance was nearly 4-fold lower compared to adults (94 mL/hour in healthy
   adults) and mean AUC was predicted to be 25% higher than adults during the dosing interval
   (mean week 24 AUC0 to 168 = 5700 nanograms (ng) x hour/mL; adult mean week 48 AUC0 to 168 =
   4548 ng x hour/mL) Inhibits CYP1A2 (increases theophylline, methadone levels)'),
