   (Gy) 2', 'Febrile Neutropenia: The use of pegfilgrastim demonstrated efficacy similar to that of filgras-
   tim on measures of neutropenia and neutrophil support in a randomized, open-label study of
   pediatric patients with sarcoma. Median duration of Grade 4 neutropenia was 5 days during
   chemotherapy cycle 1 with pegfilgrastim (n=37) and 6 days with filgrastim (n=6); during cycle 3,
   median durations were 7 days in both treatment groups. Febrile neutropenia was experienced
   by 68% of patients in the pegfilgrastim group and 85% of patients in the filgrastim group over
   the course of the study, and median days to ANC recovery were similar (14 days for both
   groups in cycle 1, 14 days with pegfilgrastim vs 15 days with filgrastim in cycle 3). The most
   common adverse event among those attributable to the study drugs was bone pain, which
   was experienced by 11% of patients receiving pegfilgrastim compared with 17% of patients re-
   ceiving filgrastim FDA Approved Pediatric Indication

Pegfilgrastim-apgf is indicated in children to decrease the incidence of infection, as manifested
