   needed Discontinuation of Therapy:
   Do not discontinue abruptly in patients who are physically dependent; create a patient-specific
   plan to taper gradually as no single taper schedule is appropriate for all patients. Consider de-
   creasing the dosage by no more than 10% to 25% every 2 to 4 weeks; more rapid tapers may
   be appropriate in patients who have been taking opioids for shorter periods of time. If serious
   withdrawal symptoms or increased pain occurs during the taper, consider stopping the taper
