   3% and 5% injection solutions: Administer IV through a large vein for rapid dilution 3% and 5% injection solutions: Do not mix or administer through same administration set
   with whole blood or cellular blood components 4/10
3% and 5% injection solutions: To avoid air embolism, do not connect flexible plastic contain-
   ers in series and do not use vented IV administration sets with the vent in the open position.
   Pressurization of IV solutions in flexible plastic containers (ie, to flow rates) can cause air em-
   bolism if the residual air in container is not fully evacuated', 'Inhalation

   When saline is administered by nebulization, adverse effects are uncommon at a 3% concen-
   tration Nebulization with 3% sodium chloride for bronchiolitis resulted in bronchospasm in
   1 out 377 doses administered without a bronchodilator When used at a 7% concentration,
   common adverse effects include increased cough and bronchospasm; use of a bronchodilator
