   a single dose or in divided doses over 24 hours; take with 8 ounces liquid Functional Constipation
   Liquid (1.745 g/30 mL)

   Disimpaction therapy: 4 mL/kg/day orally for 2 to 6 days 2', 'Functional Constipation
   Guidelines: According to NASPGHAN guidelines, initial treatment of functional constipation in-
   cludes education, diary use (to evaluate dietary and fluid intake, especially in patients less than
   6 months), and oral treatment in patients 6 months or older. Oral medication or occasional
   suppositories may be started in patients less than 6 months if initial treatment is ineffective.
   The recommended initial treatment of choice for fecal disimpaction is polyethylene glycol
   (PEG) or enemas. For maintenance therapy, PEG with or without electrolytes is the first-line
   treatment; if PEG is not available, the recommended replacement is lactulose. Other laxatives
   (milk of magnesia, mineral oil, and stimulant laxatives) may be considered as additional or sec-

ond-line treatments Additional expert opinion suggests that magnesium citrate may be used
   as a second-line treatment option for fecal disimpaction Duration of therapy: Initial therapy for fecal disimpaction should be 2 to 6 days. Maintenance
   therapy should be continued for at least 2 months or at least 1 month after a good response
   to therapy 3 , Medications should be weaned gradually and may need to be continued for
   months to years in some patients. Relapses are common and may be treated with mainte-
   nance or disimpaction therapy as needed 2

   Indication: Magnesium citrate oral liquid is an over-the-counter product effective for the relief
   of occasional constipation. Bowel movement typically occurs 30 minutes to 6 hours after ad-
   ministration Administration
   Take each dose with a full 8-ounce glass of liquid Do not administer within 2 hours before or after use of other medications Discard any unused product within 24 hours of opening the bottle', 'Common: Hypermagnesemia; hypophosphatemia; secondary hypocalcemia 5

