   • Prior to activation, allow vial to warm to room temperature 6
   • Prior to administration, perflutren lipid microspheres require activation by shaking for a full
   45 seconds in an apparatus (Vialmix(R) or Vialmix Radio Frequency Identification (RFID)(R)) pro-
   vided by the manufacturer. Do not use unless the full 45-second activation cycle is completed,
   and do not reactivate the vial if the full 45-second cycle was not completed. Do not reactivate a
   successfully activated vial • Activated perflutren in lipid microspheres is a homogenous milky white suspension with a
   presence of foam/bubbles and should be used immediately after activation. Resuspend the
   product by 10 seconds of hand agitation (through inverting the vial prior to product with-
   drawal from the vial) if not used within 5 minutes of activation. Activated perflutren in lipid mi-
   crospheres can be used for up to 12 hours from time of activation, but only after the micro-
   spheres are resuspended by hand agitation. Store activated perflutren in lipid microspheres at
   room temperature in original vial • Do not inject air into the vial. Withdraw product from the middle of the vial with the
   Intellipin(R) dispensing pin, the PINSYNC (vented vial adapter 13 mm), or with a 18- or 20-
   gauge syringe needle. Use the product immediately upon withdrawal from vial. Do not let the
   product stand in the syringe Definity(R) RT

