   exceeding 8 mg/mL or use available premixed solutions (4 to 8 mg/mL) 10,11,12 .', 'Not associated with respiratory depression or altered level of consciousness as with other
   antiepileptics (benzodiazepines, barbiturates). Stop infusion immediately if cardiac arrhythmia
   occurs. Ventricular arrhythmias have been reported. Concentration-dependent effect on
   seizures; higher concentrations (greater than 15 mg/L can result in seizures). Avoid in severe
   liver or renal impairment 23,5 ,6 .

   Solution Compatibility
   D5W, D10W, and NS.

   Terminal Injection Site Compatibility
   Alteplase, aminophylline, amiodarone, ampicillin, caffeine citrate, calcium chloride, calcium
   gluconate, cefazolin, cefoxitin, chloramphenicol, cimetidine, dexamethasone, digoxin, dobu-
