   fect in children and adolescents (n=321) was upper abdominal pain (6.2%) Extended-Release Tablet (Relexxii®): The most commonly reported adverse effect in pedi-
   atrics 6 years or older (n=321) was upper abdominal pain (6.2%) 27

   Extended-Release Oral Suspension (Quillivant™ XR): In a placebo-controlled trial of patients
   6 to 12 years of age with ADHD (n=45), the most commonly reported adverse effect was affect
   lability (9%). Other common adverse reactions are appetite decreased, insomnia, nausea, vom-
   iting, dyspepsia, abdominal pain, weight decreased, anxiety, dizziness, irritability, tachycardia,
