   Minimum inhibitory concentrations: Ansuvimab-zykl blocks binding of Zaire ebolavirus
   (EBOV) glycoprotein 1 (GP1) to the Neiman Pick cell receptor 1 in host cells (50% inhibitory con-
   centration (IC50), 09 mcg/mL), inhibiting virus entry into the host cell. Ansuvimab-zykl exhib-
   ited Fc-mediated Antibody Dependent Cellular Cytotoxicity (ADCC) activity against cells ex-
   pressing EBOV GP when effector cells were added. Ansuvimab-zykl neutralized Zaire ebolavirus
   Mayinga with a 50% effective concentration (EC50) of 06 mcg/mL in a live virus plaque-reduc-
   tion neutralization assay performed in Vero E6 cells and with an EC50 value of 09 mcg/mL in
   an EBOV GP lentivirus infectivity assay using HEK293 cells. Ansuvimab-zykl neutralized Zaire
   ebolavirus Makona with an EC50 value of 15 mcg/mL. Ansuvimab-zykl mediated ADCC, with
   maximal activity observed at a concentration of 03 mcg/mL Resistance patters: No nonclinical or clinical studies evaluating resistance to ansuvimab-zykl
   have been conducted Mechanism of action: Ansuvimab-zykl is a Zaire ebolavirus (EBOV) glycoprotein 1 (GP1)-di-
   rected recombinant, human IgG1(kappa) monoclonal antibody which binds to the glycan cap
   and inner chalice of the EBOV GP1 subunit. The epitope to which it binds is located within the
   receptor binding domain of EBOV consisting of amino acids LEIKKPDGS (GP residues 111–119)'),
