   The bioavailability of the extended-release tablets is lower under fasting conditions. Peak con-
   centrations reached in about 2 to 3 hours for immediate-release tablets and oral suspension
   and 5 to 8 hours for extended-release tablets Metabolism: Undergoes extensive metabolism to 14-OH clarithromycin which is microbiologi-
   cally active Excretion: Renal excretion accounts for 20% to 40% of the dose.
   Half-life: Clarithromycin and 14-OH clarithromycin elimination half-life is dose-dependant in
   adults; approximately 3 to 4 hours and 5 to 6 hours, respectively, for 250 mg every 12 hours
   and 5 to 7 hours and 7 to 9 hours, respectively, for 500 mg every 8 to 12 hours 2 ,19,60,17 .'),
(349, 'Cyanocobalamin', 'vitamin_supplement', TRUE, FALSE, FALSE, 100, 'Prior to treatment, obtain hematocrit, reticulocyte count, vitamin B12, folate, and iron levels.
