 ', 'Vitamin B12 Deficiency
   Vitamin B12 deficiency can be caused by dietary deficiencies (eg, vegan or vegetarian diets) or
   conditions that lead to vitamin B12 malabsorption (eg, autoimmune gastritis/pernicious ane-
   mia, gastrointestinal disorders and surgeries, use of metformin, proton pump inhibitors, or
   H2-blockers). Deficiency caused by malabsorption usually requires lifelong supplementation
