   ValGANciclovir Oral Suspension 90 mg/mL (225 mL) 11 :
   • Triturate 45 valGANciclovir 450 mg tablets into a fine powder in a glass mortar.

   • Slowly add 45 mL of the sodium benzoate solution * and work the powder into a smooth
   paste using a pestle. All film coating should dissolve
   • Add 50 mL of the cherry-chocolate vehicle **, mix well, and transfer to a beaker that has
   been calibrated to 225 mL with a graduated cylinder.

   • Rinse mortar and pestle with two 50 mL portions of the cherry-chocolate vehicle and transfer
   the liquid from each rinse into the beaker.

   • 10N hydrochloric acid should be added to adjust pH to approximately 2. This may require
   the addition of 4 to 45 mL of the 10Nhydrochloric acid.
   • Add cherry-chocolate vehicle to bring the final volume to 225 mL.

   • Add more 10Nhydrochloric acid, if necessary, to adjust the pH to approximately 2

   • Mix well and transfer the preparation to an amber bottle.

   • Label "Refrigerate," "Shake Well," and "Cytotoxic Drug Precautions."
   • Stable for at least 125 days when refrigerated (2°to 8°C)

   * In a glass beaker, dissolve 117 mg of sodium benzoate in 45 mL of Sterile Water for
   Irrigation, USP and set aside. Sodium benzoate concentration of the final suspension was 1%.

   ** Using a 500 mL graduated cylinder, add 6 mL of artificial cherry flavoring to 300 mL of
