   •Use a 20- to 24-gauge needle on an empty syringe; insert into synovial cavity and withdraw a
   few drops of synovial fluid to confirm needle placement. Replace aspirating syringe with sy-
   ringe containing betamethasone dose Intralesional Injection

   •Determine volume needed to deliver drug throughout lesion 14
   •Infantile hemangioma: Inject directly into lesion, around the edge of the lesion, or both, using a
   27- or 30-gauge needle; multiple injections at different sites may be needed for a single lesion.
   Advance needle tip into lesion, withdraw plunger gently, and if no blood returns, slowly inject
   the steroid over 1 minute. Apply pressure to stop any bleeding •Other skin lesions: Inject intradermally (not subQ) using tuberculin syringe with 25 gauge 25
   inch needle; take care to deposit uniformly IM
   •May be mixed with 1% or 2% lidocaine (without parabens) prior to use. Do not inject lidocaine
