   General Information
   • Avoid direct contact with broken or crushed tablets or oral suspension. If contact with skin or
   mucous membranes occurs, wash thoroughly with soap and water, and rinse eyes thoroughly
   with water Oral

   Tablets
   • Administer oral tablets on an empty stomach or with a low-fat meal (about 400 calories, with
   about 25% of calories from fat) • Swallow tablets whole; do not crush or divide Suspension

   • Administer oral suspension on an empty stomach Gastrostomy Tube

   Suspension
   • For patients who cannot swallow, oral suspension can be administered by enteral tube (naso-
   gastric or gastrostomy tubes) • Draw up prescribed dose with a calibrated catheter-tip syringe, and utilize this syringe to ad-
   minister the dose via the enteral tube. Refill the catheter-tip syringe with 3 mL of water, shake,
   and administer the contents via the enteral tube. Flush with water before and after enteral ad-
