   Opioid dependence, Maintenance
   Subdermal implant
   16 years or older: Insert 4 single-rod implants (each containing 2 mg of buprenorphine)
   subdermally into the inner side of the upper arm. Removal is required after 6 months. Four
   new implants may be inserted into other arm at time of removal. If implants are not inserted
   on the day of removal, initiate transmucosal buprenorphine at the patient''s previous dosage After implants have been inserted once into each arm, transition back to transmucosal
   buprenorphine. Do not reinsert into previously-used sites or sites other than the upper arm Supplemental doses of buprenorphine may be necessary; promptly evaluate patient; do not
   give prescriptions for as-needed transmucosal buprenorphine; if use of supplemental doses is
   ongoing, consider alternative buprenorphine products for maintenance treatment Expelled implant: Determine if entire 26 mm implant was expelled, then dispose of properly;
   may insert replacement implant(s) in same arm, either laterally or medially to the unexpelled
   implants, or may place in the contralateral arm Concomitant medications: Consider prescribing naloxone for the emergency treatment of
   opioid overdose when initiating and renewing treatment with buprenorphine. Also consider
   prescribing naloxone if the patient has household members (including children) or other close
   contacts at risk for accidental ingestion or opioid overdose 6

