   Injection (0.3 mg/mL)

   May be administered by slow IV injection, over at least 2 minutes, or by deep IM injection Subdermal implant
   Insertion

   Healthcare providers must receive instruction, training, and certification, prior to inserting or
   removing the implants Using aseptic technique, insert implants via applicator in a close fan-shaped distribution 4 to 6
   mm apart just under the skin of the inner upper arms (3 to 4 mm below skin); the fan shape
   should open toward the shoulder and there should be at least 5 mm between the incision and
   the implant; apply pressure for 5 minutes 5
   Verify placement after insertion via palpation. If unable to verify all 4 implants via palpation,
   use ultrasound or MRI. Implants cannot be seen via X-ray or CT scan 5
   Removal

   Verify placement prior to removal via palpation. If unable to verify all 4 implants via palpation,
   use ultrasound or MRI. Implants cannot be seen via X-ray or CT scan 5

   •Under aseptic conditions and after adequate anesthesia, make a 7 to 10 mm incision with a
   scalpel, parallel to the axis of the arm, between the second and third implants, grasp the cen-
   ter of the implant and remove; apply pressure for 5 minutes •Handle removed implants with appropriate security and accountability measures, as they will
   contain a significant amount of residual buprenorphine. Dispose of the removed implant in
   keeping with local, state, and federal regulations Sublingually

   After administration sublingually, place a pacifier in the infant''s mouth. For a volume of the
   dose greater than 5 mL, give in 2 administrations separated by at least 2 minutes', 'Injection
