   Preparation
   Extemporaneous oral compounds

   Note: A 20 mg/mL oral suspension is commercially available

   25 mg/mL Suspension (60 mL) 4
   • .Weigh out 5 g of carBAMazepine active pharmaceutical ingredient and add to a low-actinic
   prescription bottle.

   • Add SyrSpend SF PH4 using a volumetric pipette to achieve a final volume of 300 mL; mix
   well.
   • Label the container with "Shake well before using."

   • Stable for 90 days at room temperature (20 to 25°C) or under refrigeration (2 to 8°C).

   40 mg/mL Suspension (100 mL) 5
   • Triturate twenty 200 mg tablets of carBAMazepine to a fine powder using a mortar and
   pestle.

• Add enough simple syrup in geometric proportions to obtain a final volume of 100 mL; mix
   well after each addition.

   • Transfer suspension to an amber glass bottle or unit-dose oral syringes.

   • Label the container with "Shake well before using."

   • Stable for 90 days or under refrigeration (4°C).

