   Intravenous

   • Can be administered undiluted or can be diluted to a concentration of 1 to 1 mg/mL in NS
   for intravenous infusion 44,45,46,47 .

   Ophthalmic insert

   • Do not use if pouch has been damaged or opened. Do not resterilize • If necessary, dilate the punctum with an ophthalmic dilator. If perforation of punctum occurs
   do not place the insert • After drying the punctal area, use blunt forceps to grasp the insert and place into the lower
   lacrimal canaliculus by pulling the lid temporally and inserting nasally • If the insert begins to hydrate before fully inserted, discard the product and use a new insert • To aid in hydration of the insert, 1 to 2 drops of balanced salt solution may be instilled into
   the punctum • The insert is resorbable and does not require removal. If necessary, saline irrigation or man-
   ual expression can be performed to remove the insert Ophthalmic suspension

   • Shake well before use Oral
