   Mechanism of Action
   DexAMETHasone is a synthetic adrenocortical steroid with potent anti-inflammatory effects in
   disorders of many organ systems. DexAMETHasone lacks the sodium-retaining property of
   naturally occurring glucocorticoids (cortisone and hydrocortisone) Bioavailability: Injectable dexAMETHasone sodium phosphate administered orally was not
   bioequivalent to dexAMETHasone oral concentrate in 11 healthy adults; although it missed the
   bioequivalent margin (90% CI, 80% to 125%) by only a few points. The 90% CIs for ratio of
   means were 8% to 9% for AUC (0 to t), 79% to 2% for AUC (0 to infinity), and 8% to 7% for Cmax Plasma concentrations: In 21 of 189 plasma samples obtained from patients following the
