   administered via a nasogastric (NG) tube with a minimum size of 8 French NG tube (1.7 mm in-
   terior diameter) 3 ,7 .

   Use appropriate precautions for the preparation and handling of teratogenic agents 3 , Intravenous
   Avoid direct contact of the prepared intravenous solution with skin or mucous membrane. If
   contact occurs, wash skin thoroughly with soap and water and rinse eyes with plain water.
   Administer by IV infusion over at least 2 hours 7 at a final concentration of 6 mg/mL 27 in D5W.
   Do not administer by rapid or bolus IV injection Use precautionary measures appropriate for the handling and preparation of teratogenic
