   Monitoring
   Monitor blood pressure and heart rate continuously during administration. Monitoring of pul-
   monary capillary wedge pressure is required in many cases 6 ,7 . Monitor cardiovascular status
   and clinical condition with the use of nitroglycerin intraanal ointment in patients at risk for car-
   diovascular disorders', '', 'Pharmacology
   Nitroglycerin, an organic nitrate, is a vasodilating agent that relieves tension on vascular
   smooth muscle and dilates peripheral veins and arteries, particularly the veins. Intraanal appli-
   cation of nitroglycerin reduces sphincter tone and resting intraanal pressure. In a clinical trial,
   the average absolute bioavailability applied to the anal canal as a 2% ointment was approxi-
   mately 50% of the 75 mg nitroglycerin dose. Volume of distribution is approximately 3 L/kg.
   Metabolize by a liver reductase enzyme to glycerol di- and mono-nitrate metabolites and ulti-
   mately to glycerol and organic nitrate. Serum half-life is approximately 3 minutes, and ob-
   served clearance rate is approximately 1 L/kg/min 22 , 6 , 6/9'),
