   Pediatric FDA Approved Indication:

   Obiltoxaximab is indicated for the treatment of inhalational anthrax due to Bacillus anthracis in
   conjunction with appropriate antibiotic therapy. It is also indicated for inhalational anthrax
   prophylaxis when alternative agents are not available or appropriate Limitations of Use
   • Efficacy is based solely on animal models, as it is not ethical or feasible to conduct controlled
   studies in humans • Safety and pharmacokinetics have been studied in healthy adults; no studies have been con-
   ducted in pediatric patients. Pediatric dosing was derived from population pharmacokinetic
   modeling • Obiltoxaximab is not directly antibacterial and is to be used in combination with appropriate
   antibiotic therapy .

   • Obiltoxaximab does not cross the blood-brain barrier and does not prevent or treat meningi-
   tis .

