   Limitations of Use
   Immediate-release oral suspension and tablets should not be used in patients with pneu-
   monia who are judged to be in appropriate for oral therapy because of moderate to severe ill-
   ness or risk factors such as any of the following 37 :
   ●    Patients with cystic fibrosis
   ●    Patients with nosocomial infections
   ●    Patients with known or suspected bacteremia
   ●    Patients requiring hospitalization
   ●    Elderly or debilitated patients
   ●    Patients with significant underlying health problems that may compromise their ability to
        respond to their illness (including immunodeficiency or functional asplenia)

