   Aplastic Anemia; Severe
   2 years or older: 5 mg/kg/day orally in divided doses every 12 hours. Treat for 6 months, then
   taper and discontinue drug 5 ,6 ,7 .

   Atopic Dermatitis; Refractory: 5 to 6 mg/kg/day orally in 2 divided doses. Higher initial
   doses lead to more rapid symptom control 8 , Duration: Tailor to patient. Both a 12-month course and intermittent 3-month or 6-month
   courses are efficacious, with the 12-month providing better efficacy and longer lasting effects Dosage Adjustment
   Renal Dysfunction: Reduce dose by 1 mg/kg/day if creatinine increases greater than 25%
   above baseline. Follow-up in 2 to 4 weeks. Hold at lower dose if creatinine concentration is
   within 25% of baseline. Discontinue, if creatinine remains greater than 25% above baseline Graft-Versus-Host Disease (GVHD); Prophylaxis
   6 months or older: after initial IV therapy, 6 to 10 mg/kg/day orally in divided doses every 12
   hours; titrate to achieve recommended target trough blood concentrations as per local proto-
   col 10 , 11 , 12 , 13 , In clinical studies, cycloSPORINE was tapered starting at 2 months and usually
