   • Perform screening for hepatitis B virus, hepatitis C virus, human T-lymphotrophic virus 1 and
   2, and HIV 1 and 2 in accordance with clinical guidelines prior to collection of cells for manufac-
   turing • Confirm patient is appropriate for hematopoietic stem cell transplantation Childhood cerebral X-linked adrenoleukodystrophy (CALD)

   Boys, 4 years or older
   Pretreatment
   • Patients are required to undergo hematopoietic stem cell transplantation mobilization and
   apheresis to capture CD34+ cells for elivaldogene autotemcel manufacturing • Collect a minimum target number of CD34+ cells of 12 x 10(6) CD34+ cells/kg 1
   • A back-up collection of CD34+ cells of 5 x 10(6) or greater CD34+ cells/kg (if collected by
   apheresis) or 1 x 10(8) or greater Total Nucleated Cells/kg (if collected by bone marrow har-
   vest) is required • Full myeloablative and lymphodepleting conditioning must be administered prior to infusion
   of elivaldogene autotemcel • Do not begin conditioning until elivaldogene autotemcel has been received and stored at the
   treatment center and the back-up collection of CD34+ cells is confirmed • Allow a minimum of 48 hours of washout after completion of conditioning prior to infusion of
   elivaldogene autotemcel Prophylaxis
   • Prophylaxis for seizures, hepatic veno-occlusive disease, and antifungal agents and antibi-
   otics were used in clinical trials 1

Dosage
   • Minimum recommended dose: 5 x 10(6) CD34+ cells/kg; dose is based on patient weight
   prior to first apheresis 1

   • Dose may be contained in 1 or 2 patient-specific infusion bags Following Administration

   • Irradiate any blood products within the first 3 months after infusion • A granulocyte colony stimulating factor was administered in a clinical trial beginning on day 5
   following elivaldogene autotemcel administration', '• Elivaldogene autotemcel is indicated to slow the progression of neurologic dysfunction in
