   eral or posterolateral abdominal wall, insert entire length of needle perpendicularly into skin
   fold, and push the plunger rod firmly as far as it will go to inject entire contents of syringe.
   Alternate injection sites between left and right sides for each injection Discard syringes after use 3/9
Preparation, Prefilled Syringes

   • Available in single-dose, prefilled syringes affixed with an automatic needle protection sys-
   tem, however patient-specific doses may be prepared by a pharmacist under aseptic condi-
   tions if necessary • Do not mix with other medications or solutions • Do not expel air bubble from prefilled syringe prior to injection Preparation, Patient-Specific Doses
   • Determine the total dose and volume required per the duration of treatment. If the volume
   of the total required dose is less than 5 mL, use 1 prefilled syringe to prepare doses; if 5 mL
   or more, use 2 prefilled syringes. Do not pool together more than 2 prefilled syringes and do
   not combine prefilled syringes of different concentrations • Dispense the full contents of prefilled syringe(s) into a sterile, closed/sealed, empty glass vial
   (5 mL). Using sterile graduated tuberculin syringes with 27 gauge x 1/2 inch needles, withdraw
   required dose from vial and replace needle cap over needle; repeat process to prepare appro-
   priate number of doses. Discard prefilled syringes and any unused portion in vial • Store prepared tuberculin syringes in refrigerator between 36 and 46°F (2 to 8°C); do not
