   methotrexate clearance 3 :

●   Falsely elevated plasma methotrexate concentration may occur during or shortly after the
        end of a high-dose methotrexate infusion due to contamination if the specimen is drawn
        from the same lumen of the central venous catheter used for the infusion. If the plasma
        methotrexate concentration is elevated, but serum creatinine is normal, repeat the mea-
        surement with a new blood sample.
    ●   Rebound of methotrexate concentrations may occur more than 48 hours after glucarpidase
        administration due to release of methotrexate from tissue stores. Therefore, continue mon-
        itoring methotrexate concentrations.
    ●   An immunoassay method that does not distinguish between methotrexate and the DAMPA
        metabolite overestimates the true methotrexate concentration. Immunoassay interference
        and an inability to accurately quantify the methotrexate concentration lasts for approxi-
        mately 48 hours after glucarpidase.
    ●   When using a high pressure liquid chromatography method that chromatographically sepa-
        rates methotrexate from the DAMPA metabolite, the plasma methotrexate concentration
        usually drops by more than 95% by 15 minutes after glucarpidase.', 'Monitoring in patients with high-dose methotrexate-induced acute kidney injury and delayed', 'Total body: 5 mL/min (healthy subjects); Renal impairment, similar to healthy subjects 4

