   Monitoring
   Toxic Laboratory Monitoring

   • Verify pregnancy status in females of reproductive potential before treatment initiation • Perform a CBC with differential and platelet counts, hepatic enzymes, renal function tests,
   and chest X-ray at baseline 25,26,27,28,29 .

• Obtain blood counts and monitor liver and renal tests periodically during treatment and as
   clinically indicated When treating arthritis or psoriasis, monitor hematology at least monthly
   and renal and liver function every 1 to 2 months during therapy for arthritis and psoriasis.
   More frequent monitoring may be indicated during therapy initiation or dose changes and
   when there is an increased risk of elevated methotrexate blood levels (eg, dehydration)
   25,26,27,28,29
                     .

   • Transient elevations of liver enzymes are frequently observed, however persistently abnor-
   mal liver function tests and/or depression of serum albumin may indicate liver toxicity. During
   therapy perform liver biopsy if there are persistently abnormal liver function test values, or a
   decrease in serum albumin below the normal range for well-controlled RA patients 26 , 27 , 28 , • Monitor serum methotrexate levels in patients with significant third space compartment ac-
   cumulations (eg, plural effusion, ascites) 25,26,27,28,29 .

   Toxic Physical Monitoring

