Oral/intravenous moxifloxacin is not approved in pediatric patients Administration
   Intravenous: Administer IV solution (1.6 mg/mL) over 60 minutes Ophthalmic: For topical ophthalmic use only. Do not touch the dropper tip to any surface to
   avoid contaminating the contents 23 , Oral

   • Give with or without food, with a generous amount of fluid • Administer at least 4 hours before or 8 hours after products containing magnesium, alu-
   minum, iron, or zinc, including antacids, sucralfate, multivitamins, and didanosine-buffered
   tablets for oral suspension or powder for oral solution • Missed dose: Administer anytime up to 8 hours prior to the next scheduled dose. If less than
   8 hours remain before the next dose, do not administer the missed dose and continue treat-
   ment with the next scheduled dose. Do not administer double doses to compensate for a
   missed dose • TB: Directly observed therapy (DOT) is generally recommended in all cases, especially with in-
   termittent (not daily) dosage regimens Preparation

   Extemporaneous oral compound

   20 mg/mL suspension (60 mL) 25

   • Thoroughly levigate three 400 mg tablets of moxifloxacin to a fine powder in a glass mortar.
   Sieve powder from enteric coating remnants.

   • Mix 30 mL Ora-Plus and 30 mL of either Ora-Sweet or Ora-Sweet SF for a total volume of 60
   mL.
   • Levigate 30 mL of the Ora-Plus and Ora-Sweet/Ora-Sweet SF mixture into powder using 2
   geometric dilutions until a smooth suspension has formed.
   • Transfer to a 2 ounce amber bottle; rinse the contents of the mortar into the bottle using the
   remaining Ora-Plus and Ora-Sweet/Ora-Sweet SF mixture for a final volume of 60 mL.

   • Label with "shake well" and an expiration date 90 days after preparation.', 'Ophthalmic

