   Hepatitis B virus (HBV) reactivation can occur in patients receiving obinutuzumab or other
   CD20-directed cytolytic antibodies, which can progress to life-threatening or fatal fulminant
   hepatitis or hepatic failure. Screen patients at baseline for HBV infection. Monitor HBV-positive
   patients during and after treatment with obinutuzumab. If HBV reactivation occurs, discon-
   tinue obinutuzumab and concomitant medications. Life-threatening or fatal progressive multi-
   focal leukoencephalopathy has also been reported Monitoring
