Mechanism of action: Pantoprazole inhibits gastric acid secretion by inhibition of hydrogen-
creases Protein-binding: Approximately 98% (mainly to albumin) Metabolism: Extensively metabolized in the liver by CYP2C19 and CYP3A4 isoenzymes.', 'Pharmacology
   Mechanism of action: Pantoprazole inhibits gastric acid secretion by inhibition of hydrogen-
   potassium ATPase, the enzyme responsible for the final step in the secretion of hydrochloric
   acid by the gastric parietal cell ("proton pump"). Antisecretory activity persists for greater than
   24 hours 3 , Time to effect: Maximal effect may take 3 to 5 days to achieve Bioavailability: Approximately 50% with the tablet formulation in a pharmacokinetic study in
   children 13 ; however, in adults, the bioavailability is approximately 77%. Oral formulations are

bioequivalent; however, food reduces the bioavailability of the delayed-release suspension,
   but not the delayed-release tablet.
   Tmax: Peak concentration is reached in approximately 2 to 5 hours after oral administration
   and 30 minutes after IV administration. Cmax and AUC increase proportionally as dose in-
   creases Protein-binding: Approximately 98% (mainly to albumin) Metabolism: Extensively metabolized in the liver by CYP2C19 and CYP3A4 isoenzymes.
   Polymorphism may be displayed with the CYP2C19 isoenzyme, leading to poor metabolizers of
   the drug. In 1 pharmacokinetic study, poor metabolizers (n=3) had a 6- to 14-fold increase in
   AUC and a 10-fold increase in half-life compared with extensive metabolizers Elimination: Urine (71%) and feces (18%) Clearance: Apparent oral clearance (L/hr/kg) is highest in the 1 to 6 years age range (1.3 to 1), with lower values in infants 1 to 12 months (0.8 to 5) 1 , and children 6 years and older
   (0.18 to 41) Half-life: Mean half-lives are approximately 4 to 8 hours and 7 to 9 hours in pediatric
   patients aged 1 month to 6 years 1 and 6 to 16 years, respectively Obesity: Population pharmacokinetics-derived parameters were estimated in 37 obese (body
   mass index 95th percentile for age or more) children after a single dose of pantoprazole de-
   layed-release tablet. Data from a CYP2C19 poor metabolizer were excluded 15 :
