   occur within the first few days and improve as dermatitis resolves An open-label, random-
   ized study (n=2418) demonstrated no difference in the growth rate, incidence of bacterial or vi-
   ral infections, or development of immune system in infants (3 months or older but less than 12
   months) between topical pimecrolimus or topical corticosteroids as needed over a 5-year pe-
   riod for atopic dermitis. Bronchitis, infected eczema, impetigo, and nasopharyngitis occurred
   more often in the pimecrolimus group. The median duration of treatment was 5 days for
   pimecrolimus compared with 178 days for topical corticosteroids 2/4
