   Rifampin: Do not exceed 2 mg/day 1', 'Pitavastatin 1 mg/day, 2 mg/day, and 4 mg/day significantly reduced total cholesterol, LDL-C,
   non-HDL-C, and apolipoprotein B levels compared with placebo in a randomized, 12-week
   study of pediatric patients 8 to 16 years old with heterozygous familial hypercholesterolemia
   (HeFH; N=82). Triglyceride and HDL levels were not significantly changed. Included patients
   had genetically confirmed HeFH, a fasting LDL-C of 190 mg/dL or greater, or a fasting LDL-C of
   160 mg/dL or greater plus 1 additional cardiovascular risk factor. Mean baseline LDL-C was 235
