   Administration
   Oral route
   Delayed release tablets

   • Swallow tablets whole. Do not crush, chew, or divide 1

   • Administer with or without food 3
   • For those who cannot eat a full meal, delayed-release tablets should be used instead of oral
   suspension for the prophylaxis indication. Delayed-release tablets generally provide higher
   plasma drug exposures than oral suspension under both fed and fasted conditions PowderMix for Delayed release suspension

   • Administer reconstituted suspension using the provided 3-mL green syringe if dose is 3 mL or
   less. Use the provided 10-mL blue syringe if dose is more than 3 mL. Administer with food. Do
   not administer with alcohol. The reconstituted suspension must be used within 1 hour.
   Discard unused portion of the prepared drug product • Each single-use packet contains 300 mg of posaconazole to be suspended in 9 mL of mixing
   liquid giving a final concentration of approximately 30 mg/mL 2
   Suspension

   • Shake well prior to use and administer with measured dosing spoon • Administer during or immediately (within 20 minutes) following a full meal. For those who
   cannot eat a full meal administer with a liquid nutritional supplement or acidic carbonated
   beverage (eg, ginger ale) Pharmacokinetic studies demonstrate higher posaconazole trough
   concentrations when administered with a fatty meal Intravenous
   • Administer using a 22-micron polyethersulfone (PES) or polyvinylidene difluoride (PVDF) fil-
   ter. Give by slow IV infusion over 90 minutes via a central venous line (including a central ve-
   nous catheter or peripherally inserted central catheter (PICC)) • If a central venous catheter is unavailable, a single dose may be given by slow IV infusion over
   30 minutes via peripheral venous catheter. If multiple doses are to be given, a central line is re-
   quired 7/22
