   • Concomitant medications (if CSF protein 1 g/dL or greater or presence of focal lesions
   with substantial mass effect): Consider adding corticosteroids, for as short a duration as
   clinically feasible • Duration: At least 6 weeks; longer duration may be necessary if extensive clinical or radio-
   logic disease or if response is incomplete at 6 weeks 2

   Acquired toxoplasmosis - HIV co-infection; Secondary prophylaxis

   • Guideline dosage: 5 to 60 mg/kg orally twice daily; MAX 2 to 4 g/day 2
   • Concomitant medications: Pyrimethamine 1 mg/kg orally once daily OR 15 mg/m2 orally
   once daily PLUS folinic acid (leucovorin) 5 mg orally once every 3 days 2

   • Discontinuation, children 1 to less than 6 years: May consider with at least 6 months of
   stable combination antiretroviral therapy (cART) and CD4 percentage 15% or greater for at
   least 6 months 2

