   Observe injection site for pain, erythema, and induration (common).', '', 'Pharmacology
   Tdap vaccines are aluminum-salt-adsorbed preparations. They contain tetanus toxoid, diph-
   theria toxoid, and pertussis antigens. All acellular pertussis vaccines contain inactivated per-
   tussis toxoid, but vary in the inclusion and concentration of four other pertussis antigens.
   Compared with DTaP vaccines, Tdap vaccines contain the same antigens but in reduced quan-
   tities. Tetanus and diphtheria toxoids are prepared by formaldehyde treatment of the respec-
   tive toxins. Each dose of Adacel® contains 5 Lf tetanus toxoid, 2 Lf diphtheria toxoid, 5 mcg
   detoxified pertussis toxin, 5 mcg FHA, 3 mcg pertactin, and 5 mcg fimbriae types 2 and 3, with 3 mg 2-phenoxyethanol (not as a preservative), and aluminum phosphate as the adjuvant.
   Each dose of Boostrix® contains 5 Lf tetanus toxoid, 5 Lf diphtheria toxoid, 8 mcg detoxified
   pertussis toxin, 8 mcg FHA, and 5 mcg of pertactin with aluminum phosphate as the adju-
   vant. A serum antitoxin level of at least 1 international units/mL is considered protective for
   both tetanus and diphtheria, although a level of 01 international units/mL is considered the
   minimum protective level. Seroprotection rates for tetanus and diphtheria (0.1 international
   units/mL or greater by ELISA) are 99% to 100% post-vaccination. The booster response rates to
   the pertussis antigens with Tdap vaccines have been shown to be comparable with those for
   DTaP vaccines, and pertussis antibody geometric mean concentrations following Tdap vac-

cines were noninferior to those following a primary vaccination series with DTaP vaccines
   12,13
