   Perform periodic radiologic imaging (typically CT) and serial clinical evaluations to determine
   resolution of invasive aspergillosis For candidemia, monitor blood cultures daily or every other day until Candida is cleared Toxic Monitoring
   Assess liver function tests and bilirubin at baseline and at least weekly for the first month of
   voriconazole therapy. If the patient is clinically stable, then the frequency of monitoring liver
   function and bilirubin tests may be reduced to monthly during therapy. Monitor pancreatic
   function in patients with risk factors for acute pancreatitis, including recent chemotherapy or
   hematopoietic stem cell transplantation. Assess renal function and monitor for elevations in
   serum creatinine during voriconazole therapy. Oral voriconazole is recommended in patients
   with moderate to severe renal dysfunction (CrCl less than 50 mL/minute). If IV dosing is neces-
   sary in these patients, close monitoring is required due to the possibility of accumulation of
   the IV vehicle, sulfobutyl ether beta-cyclodextrin (SBECD) . Assess visual function (visual acuity,
   visual field, and color perception) if voriconazole therapy continues beyond 28 days. Monitor
