   Mechanism of action
   Allopurinol sodium and its metabolite, oxypurinol (alloxanthine), decrease the production of
   uric acid by inhibiting the action of xanthine oxidase, the enzyme that converts hypoxanthine
   to xanthine and xanthine to uric acid. Allopurinol sodium also increases reutilization of hypox-
   anthine and xanthine for nucleotide and nucleic acid synthesis. Allopurinol thereby decreases
   uric acid concentrations in both serum and urine by inhibiting uric acid formation Oxypurinol, which is in systemic circulation at much higher concentrations and much longer
   time period than allopurinol, exerts the main pharmacologic effect. The pharmacokinetic pa-
