although similar increases in exposure are seen with concomitant use of CYP2D6 inhibitors', 'Pharmacology
   Atomoxetine is a selective norepinephrine reuptake inhibitor; its mechanism of effect in ADHD
   is not known. Well-absorbed, minimally affected by food, and has 63% absolute bioavailability
   in extensive metabolizers and 94% in poor metabolizers. Peak levels at 1 to 2 hours after oral
   administration. Approximately 98% bound to plasma proteins. Primarily eliminated through
   oxidation by CYP2D6 isoenzymes and subsequent glucuronidation. Half-life is approximately 5
   hours. Those patients classified as CYP2D6 poor metabolizers (2% of African Americans and
   7% of Caucasians) have a 10-fold higher AUCs, 5-fold higher peak concentrations, and slower
   elimination (half-life of approximately 24 hours) than those with normal activity of this enzyme,
   although similar increases in exposure are seen with concomitant use of CYP2D6 inhibitors
   (eg, fluoxetine, paroxetine) in these patients. When normalized on a mg/kg basis, Cmax, Vd,
   AUC, clearance and half-life are similar in children, adolescents, and adults'),
