   A single subQ injection of canakinumab was associated with higher rates of adapted juvenile
   idiopathic arthritis American College of Rheumatology 30 (JIA ACR 30) responses at day 15
   (84% vs 10%) and day 29 (81% vs 10%) compared with placebo, in a phase 3, randomized, dou-
   ble-blind, controlled trial (n=84). During the 12 to 32 week open-label phase (n=177), a de-

creased dosage or discontinuation of glucocorticoid therapy compared with placebo was ob-
   served and fewer disease flares compared with placebo (26% vs 75%) during a withdrawal
   phase (n=100). Efficacy cannot be generalized to patients who have SJIA without fever Pediatric Approved FDA Indications

   Indicated for the treatment of the following autoinflammatory Periodic Fever Syndromes: 5
   ●       Cryopyrin-Associated Periodic Syndromes (CAPS) in patients 4 years and older
   ●       Tumor Necrosis Factor Receptor Associated Periodic Syndrome (TRAPS)
   ●       Hyperimmunoglobulin D Syndrome (HIDS)/Mevalonate Kinase Deficiency (MKD)
   ●       Familial Mediterranean Fever (FMF)

   Canakinumab is also indicated for the treatment of active systemic juvenile idiopathic arthritis
   in patients 2 years of age and older Administration
   Reconstitute each vial by slowly injecting 1 mL of sterile water for injection using an 18-gauge
   2-inch needle 5
   Swirl vial slowly at an angle of about 45 degrees for approximately 1 minute and let stand for 5
   minutes Gently turn vial upside down and back again 10 times and allow vial to stand at room tempera-
   ture for 15 minutes to obtain a clear solution. Do not shake; slight foaming of solution may oc-
   cur 5
   Solution should be clear to opalescent and colorless or may have a slight brownish-yellow tint Reconstituted solution will have a concentration of 150 mg/mL Do not use if particulate matter is present or if solution has a distinctly brown color If solution is not used within 60 minutes, it may be stored in the refrigerator at 2 to 8 degrees
   C (36 to 46 degrees F) and used within 4 hours For subQ use only; administer through 27-gauge 5-inch needle 5

