   Candesartan is an angiotensin receptor blocker which blocks the vasoconstrictor and aldos-
   terone-secreting effects of angiotensin II by selectively blocking the binding of angiotensin II to
   the AT1 receptor in many tissues, such as vascular smooth muscle and the adrenal gland. Its
   action is independent of the pathways for angiotensin II synthesis. Does not inhibit an-
   giotensin converting enzyme (ACE) and therefore does not affect response to bradykinin like
   ACE inhibitors. Bioavailability is approximately 15% and does not appear to be affected by
   food. Peak concentration reached in approximately 4 hours after administration. Highly bound
   to plasma proteins (greater than 99%) and does not penetrate red blood cells. Metabolized
   rapidly and completely by ester hydrolysis in the intestinal tract during absorption. Primarily
   eliminated in the urine (26% unchanged drug) and feces via bile (approximately 67%) Elimination half-life in children is approximately 7 to 7 hours 4 ,5 .'),
