via inhibition of cell-wall synthesis, with a wide range of activity against many gram-positive', 'Pharmacology
   Cefpodoxime proxetil is a broad-spectrum, third-generation cephalosporin that is bactericidal
   via inhibition of cell-wall synthesis, with a wide range of activity against many gram-positive
   and gram-negative organisms. It is a prodrug which is de-esterified to the active metabolite
   cefpodoxime. Bioavailability is approximately 50%. Food increases the absorption of the
   tablets but does not significantly affect the absorption of the suspension. Peak levels attained
   approximately 2 to 3 hours after dosing. Widely distributed in body tissues; volume of distribu-
   tion is higher in younger children (1.52 L/kg) compared with older children (0.89 L/kg). Protein
   binding is approximately 20% to 30%. Primarily eliminated through renal excretion. Elimination
   half-life is approximately 2 to 3 hours in children and prolonged in patients with renal impair-
   ment 1 ,2 ,17 .'),
