   CYP3A4 Cancer in children (n=28), treated with approximately 10 mg/kg/day of fluconazole, was associ-
   ated with lower fluconazole trough concentrations (median 6 mg/L vs 1 mg/L) than chil-
   dren without cancer in a retrospective study of critically ill children (N=99) treated with a me-
   dian of 10 mg/kg/day. Additionally, fluconazole trough concentration increased as the flucona-
   zole dose, weight, or serum urea concentration increased. Children treated with esomeprazole
