    ●   Hematologic Toxicity: Granulocytopenia, anemia, thrombocytopenia, and pancytopenia
        have been reported in patients treated with ganciclovir sodium.
    ●   Impairment of Fertility: Based on animal data and limited human data, ganciclovir sodium
        may cause temporary or permanent inhibition of spermatogenesis in males and suppres-
        sion of fertility in females.
    ●   Fetal Toxicity: Based on animal data, ganciclovir sodium has the potential to cause birth
        defects in humans
    ●   Mutagenesis and Carcinogenesis: Based on animal data, ganciclovir sodium has the po-
