   • Stable for 3 to 9 months at room temperature with a 5% loss in chemical activity over the first
   3 months and no subsequent loss until 9 months', 'Common: The most commonly reported adverse reactions in pediatric patients were infec-
   tions (39.8%), neutropenia (12.6% to 13%), fever (7.7%), thrombocytopenia (7.4% to 9%),
