   Administration
   Chewable dispersible tablets: Administer entire tablets only. Round doses down to the near-
   est whole tablet. May be swallowed whole, chewed, or dispersed in water or diluted fruit juice.
   Disperse by adding tablets to a small amount of liquid (1 teaspoon, or enough to cover the
   medication). When tablets are completely dispersed (approximately 1 minute), swirl solution
   and consume entire volume immediately Extended-release tablets: Administer once daily, with or without food. Swallow whole; do not
   chew, crush, or divide Orally disintegrating tablets: Place onto tongue and move around in the mouth. May be
   swallowed with or without water. May be administered with or without food Oral suspension:
   • Shake well before each use; discard any unused portion 90 days after first opening container • Use a calibrated measuring device such as an oral dosing syringe or cup to measure and de-
   liver an accurate dose; a household teaspoon or tablespoon is not an adequate measuring de-
   vice • Administer with or without food Preparation

