   Dilution of ondansetron injection is required before administration to patients for the preven-
   tion of nausea and vomiting associated with emetogenic chemotherapy. Dilution is not re-
   quired when used for the prevention of postoperative nausea and vomiting If a precipitate is observed at the stopper/vial interface in vials stored upright, mix by shaking
   the vial; potency and safety are not affected by this occasional precipitate formation Depending on the fluid needs of the patient, ondansetron injection may be diluted with 10 to
   50 mL of D5W or NS. Other compatible IV fluids which may be used for dilution include D5NS,
   D5-0.45% NaCl, or 3% NaCl Some institutions use standard concentrations of 1 and 2 mg/mL After dilution, do not use beyond 24 hours. Although ondansetron is physically and chemically
   stable for 48 hours when diluted as recommended, sterile precautions are advised because
   diluents generally do not contain preservative Extemporaneous Preparation

