   Monitoring
   Laboratory Parameters

   •Assess serum creatinine prior to each infusion •Assess urea and electrolytes prior to the first dose •Assess liver function test prior to the first dose •Monitor CBC with differential, hematocrit, and hemoglobin before the first dose 1 and for the
   first 2 weeks following the treatment in patients with preexisting anemia, leukopenia, or
   thrombocytopenia •Measure serum vitamin D concentration prior to first infusion. The concentration should be
   greater than 50 nmol/L to minimize the risk of hypocalcemia •Measure calcium, phosphate, magnesium, potassium, and serum electrolytes carefully follow-
   ing treatment initiation •Measure parathyroid hormone before the first dose •Dual energy X-ray absorptiometry at baseline and at annual intervals to assess response 1

