   patite) crystals and prevents the dissolution of this mineral in bone. It may inhibit the activity
   of osteoclasts Distribution: The mean +/- SD body retention of pamidronate was 54 +/- 16% of the dose over
   120 hours Metabolism: Not metabolized Clearance: Exclusively eliminated by the kidneys; total and renal clearances were 107 +/- 50
   mL/min and 49 +/- 28 mL/min, respectively Excretion: After administration of 30-, 60-, and 90-mg over 4 hours and 90-mg over 24 hours,
   an overall mean +/- SD of 46 +/- 16% was excreted unchanged in the urine within 120 hours.
   Cumulative urinary excretion was linearly related to dose Half-life: 28 +/- 7 hours'),
