      performed 4 to 8 weeks after switching to long-acting CAB and RPV. HIV-RNA also should
      be checked in patients with unplanned missed visits and delayed dosing of long-acting
      CAB and RPV. When viremia develops during long-acting therapy, resistance testing, in-
      cluding integrase resistance testing, should be performed. Follow-up dosing in patients
      with missed doses should not be delayed while waiting for viral load and resistance test
      results. However, regimen changes should be prompted if resistance to CAB and/or RPV is
      discovered.
