   zyme (ACE) inhibitor than benazepril. Both benazepril and benazeprilat undergo glucuronida-
   tion Excretion: Predominantly cleared by renal excretion. Nonrenal excretion is approximately
   11% to 12% of benazeprilat excretion Half-life: After a single dose, the half life was 5 hours in patients older than 1 month to 24
   months or younger (n=5), 5 hours for patients older than 2 years to 12 years or younger
