  10 to 40 mg/mL and infuse over 10 to 30 minutes', 'A life-threatening arrhythmia was reported in patients (n=6) who received a bolus administration (less than 60 sec-
  onds) of cefotaxime during post-marketing surveillance. Cefotaxime should be administered over a minimum of 3 min-
  utes. Encephalopathy and seizures have been reported, especially in patients with renal impairment receiving high
  doses. Rare cases of granulocytopenia and agranulocytosis have been reported with cefotaxime, particularly with
  longer durations of therapy. May be locally irritating to tissues if extravasation occurs. Common side effects with ther-
  apy (IV or IM injection) include local injection site reactions (4.3%), hypersensitivity reactions (2.4%), and gastrointesti-
  nal reactions (1.4%). Rarely, nausea or vomiting may occur. Pseudomembranous colitis may occur during or following
