   10 to 60 mg daily in single- and multiple-dose studies. Following a single 40-mg dose, peak
   blood levels occurred at approximately 4 hours. The relative bioavailability of oral citalopram is
   80%. Vd is approximately 12 L/kg. Plasma protein binding is approximately 80%. Undergoes
   hepatic metabolism, mainly via N-demethylation (CYP3A4 and CYP2C19 isoenzymes), deamina-
   tion, and N-oxidation. Cmax and AUC are increased by approximately 68% and 107%, respec-
