  Administration
  Oral
  Delayed-Release Capsules or Granules

  • Take with fruit juice (except grapefruit juice) or water. Avoid drinking alcohol • Administer at least 2 hours after a meal. Allow 30 minutes after administration before eating. If administration with
  food is necessary, up to 4 ounces (one-half cup) of food may be eaten within 1 hour before up to 1 hour after adminis-
  tration, but avoid high-fat food close to the administration time. Take in a consistent manner with respect to food • Swallow capsules whole; do not crush or chew capsules or oral granules. Patients with difficulty swallowing capsules
  may take with intact granules (from an opened capsule or oral granules packet) sprinkled and mixed with up to 4 ounces
  of applesauce or berry jelly, or mixed into 4 ounces of fruit juice other than grapefruit juice • Take jelly, applesauce, or juice mixture within 30 minutes of preparation. Do not save mixtures for later use • Administer at least 1 hour before or after medications containing bicarbonate or carbonate • If a dose is missed, take as soon as possible up to 8 hours after the scheduled dose. If the missed dose is within 4 hours
  of the next scheduled dose, skip the missed dose and take the next scheduled dose. Do not take 2 doses at one time to
  make up for the missed dose Immediate-Release Capsules
  • Contents of capsules may be sprinkled over food. Do not administer intact capsules to children under the age of ap-
  proximately 6 years due to risk of aspiration Gastrostomy tube
  Delayed-Release Capsules

