      phase regimens 5 days/wk for 15 doses (3 weeks), then twice weekly for 12 doses.
      d. Ethambutol may be omitted by using a 3-drug regimen (isoniazid, rifampin, pyrazi-
      namide) in pediatric patients who are HIV-uninfected, no prior TB history, live in an area
      with a low prevalence of drug-resistant TB, and do not have exposure to an individual
      from an area with a high prevalence of drug-resistant TB. Due to difficulty determining
      these criteria, the American Thoracic Society and American Academy of Pediatrics recom-
      mend using ethambutol for all patients.
      e. Ethambutol may be discontinued once susceptibility studies confirm susceptibility to
      both isoniazid and rifampin
      * Severe pulmonary TB = Chest radiograph with cavitary lesion or more than 1 lobe in-
      volvement or complex pleural effusion

