      a. Duration for extrapulmonary TB: Bone or joint disease or meningitis, consider 10-
      month continuation phase (12 months total). For drug-resistant TB, base therapy on the
      resistance pattern of the child (or of the source case where the child''s isolate is not avail-
      able); consult an expert.
      b. Regimen for minimal disease that is drug-susceptible in immunocompetent patient: 3-
      drug intensive phase regimen (exclude ethambutol) followed by 4-month continuation
      phase (6 months total duration).
