   Dose adjustments
   Adverse Reactions

   Febrile Neutropenia: 1 ,2
   ●   Grade 3: Interrupt everolimus until recovery to Grade 2 or less and no fever. Reinitiate at
       50% of the previous dose; change to every other day dosing if the reduced dose is lower
       than the lowest available strength
   ●   Grade 4: Permanently discontinue

   Metabolic Events (eg, Hyperglycemia, dyslipidemia): 1 , 2

●   Grade 3: Withhold until improvement to Grade 0, 1, or Resume at 50% of previous dose;
       change to every other day dosing if the reduced dose is lower than the lowest available
       strength
   ●   Grade 4: Permanently discontinue

   Neutropenia: 1 ,2
   ●   Grade 3: Interrupt everolimus until symptoms improve to Grade 2 or less and reinitiate at
       the same dosage
   ●   Grade 4: Interrupt everolimus until symptoms improve to Grade 2 or less and reinitiate at
       50% of the previous dose; change to every other day dosing if the reduced dose is lower
       than the lowest available strength

   Non-Hematologic Toxicities, Excluding Metabolic Events and Stomatitis: 1 ,2
   ●   Grade 2 (intolerable): Withhold until improvement to Grade 0 or Resume at same dose. If
       toxicity recurs at Grade 2, withhold until improvement to Grade 0 or Resume at 50% of
       previous dose; change to every other day dosing if the reduced dose is lower than the low-
       est available strength
   ●   Grade 3: Withhold until improvement to Grade 0 or Consider resuming at 50% of previ-
       ous dose; change to every other day dosing if the reduced dose is lower than the lowest
       available strength. If recurs at Grade 3, permanently discontinue
   ●   Grade 4: Permanently discontinue

   Noninfectious Pneumonitis: 1 , 2
   ●   Grade 2: Withhold until improvement to Grade 0 or 1 then resume at 50% of previous dose;
       change to every other day dosing if the reduced dose is lower than the lowest available
       strength. Permanently discontinue if toxicity does not resolve or improve to Grade 1 within
       4 weeks
   ●   Grade 3: Withhold until improvement to Grade 0 or Resume at 50% of previous dose;
       change to every other day dosing if the reduced dose is lower than the lowest available
       strength. If toxicity recurs at Grade 3, permanently discontinue
   ●   Grade 4: Permanently discontinue

   Stomatitis: 1 ,2
   ●   Grade 2: Withhold until improvement to Grade 0 or Resume at same dose. If recurs at
       Grade 2, withhold until improvement to Grade 0 or Resume at 50% of previous dose;
       change to every other day dosing if the reduced dose is lower than the lowest available
       strength

●   Grade 3: Withhold until improvement to Grade 0 or Resume at 50% of previous dose;
       change to every other day dosing if the reduced dose is lower than the lowest available
       strength
   ●   Grade 4: Permanently discontinue

   Thrombocytopenia: 1 ,2
   ●   Grade 2: Interrupt everolimus until symptoms improve to Grade 1 or less and reinitiate at
       the same dosage
   ●   Grade 3 or 4: Interrupt everolimus until symptoms improve to Grade 1 or less; reinitiate at
       50% of the previous dose; change to every other day dosing if the reduced dose is lower
       than the lowest available strength

   Concomitant Interacting Drugs

   Concomitant P-glycoprotein and Moderate CYP3A4 Inhibitor: 1 ,2 .
   ●   Reduce the daily dose by 50%. Change to every other day dosing if the reduced dose is
       lower than the lowest available strength.
   ●   Assess trough concentrations when initiating and discontinuing the inhibitor.
   ●   Once the inhibitor has been discontinued for 3 days, resume treatment at the dose adminis-
       tered prior to initiation of the inhibitor

   Concomitant P-glycoprotein and Strong CYP3A4 Inducer: 1 , 2
   ●   Double the daily dose in increments of 5 mg or less (multiple increments may be required).
       Addition of another strong CYP3A4 inducer in a patient already receiving treatment with a
       strong CYP3A4 inducer may not require additional dosage modification.
   ●   Assess trough concentrations when initiating and discontinuing the inhibitor.
   ●   Once all inducers have been discontinued for 5 days, resume treatment at the dose admin-
       istered prior to initiation of the inducer

   Hepatic Impairment

   Severe hepatic impairment (Child-Pugh class C): 1 ,2
