   Formoterol fumarate is a long-acting selective beta-2 adrenoceptor agonist which acts locally
   in the lung as a bronchodilator. Rapidly absorbed in the plasma reaching a peak concentration
   within 5 minutes after dosing Because of the increased lipophilicity of LABAs, the duration of
   action of bronchodilation is approximately 12 hours after a single dose; however, for chronic
