   SUBQ:

   • Each prefilled syringe, One-Press injector, or prefilled pen is for single-dose use only • Remove prefilled syringe, One-Press injector, or prefilled pen from the refrigerator and allow
   to reach up to 25° C (77° F)(30 minutes) without removing the needle cap • Solution is clear and colorless to light yellow that may contain small translucent particles; do
   not use if the liquid contains large particles, is discolored or cloudy; do not shake • A healthcare provider or caregiver should inject the dose. Inject the full amount (1 mL OR 2
   mL, which provides 100 mg OR 200 mg of guselkumab) into the front of the thighs or the lower
   abdomen except for 2 inches around the navel. For the prefilled syringe only, injection can also
   be given in the back of the upper arms. Do not inject into areas where the skin is tender,
   bruised, red, hard, thick, scaly, or affected by psoriasis • Discard any unused product • If a dose is missed, administer the dose as soon as possible. Thereafter, resume dosing at the
   regular scheduled time', 'Adult data unless otherwise specified.

