ported in adult patients who received ivermectin 100 to 200 mcg/kg (n=963) included facial
   edema (1.2%), peripheral edema (3.2%), orthostatic hypotension (1.1%), tachycardia (3.5%),
   headache (0.2%), and myalgia (0.4%) In a multicenter, cluster-randomized, double-blind, double-dummy, controlled trial (n=812)
   comparing oral ivermectin to 5% malathion lotion, a 7 year old girl in the ivermectin group
   experienced a seizure 6 days after the first dose. The patient was hospitalized and a right
   rolandic focus was found. She recovered and was discharged with a prescription for oxcar-
   bazepine. Impetigo (n=2), nausea and vomiting (n=1), gastroenteritis (n=3), and convulsions
   (n=1) were reported causes for discontinuation Topical: In a placebo-controlled trial, a single 10-minute treatment with topical ivermectin in
