   Guideline dosage

   29 days to 8 years of age: Initial, 200 mg/m2 (maximum 200 mg/dose) orally once daily for
   the first 14 days. If no rash develops, increase to 200 mg/m2 orally twice daily (maximum 200
   mg/dose). Alternatively, may initiate with twice daily frequency at 200 mg/m2 in children 2
   years or younger. In children 6 years or older, who are able to swallow the extended-release
   tablets whole and are on twice daily frequency, switch to once-daily dosing of the extended-re-
   lease tablets based on the dosing schedule below 8 years or older: Initial, 120 to 150 mg/m2 (maximum 200 mg/dose) orally once daily for the
   first 14 days. If no rash develops, increase to 120 to 150 mg/m2 orally twice daily (maximum
   200 mg/dose). May then switch to once-daily dosing of the extended-release tablets based on
   the dosing schedule below Adolescents: 200 mg orally once daily for first 14 days. If no rash develops, increase to 200 mg
   orally twice daily If therapy is interrupted for more than 14 days, dosing should be reinitiated as the once-daily
   regimen for 14 days .
