   Prevention of maternal-fetal HIV transmission: In a phase III randomized trial (n=1684), the
   combination of 6 weeks of zidovudine plus 3 doses of nevirapine or the combination of 6
   weeks of zidovudine plus nelfinavir and lamiVUDine for 2 weeks was associated with a lower
   intrapartum transmission rate when compared with zidovudine alone in infants born to
   women who received no antenatal antiretroviral therapy (2.2% versus 5% versus 9%, re-
   spectively). The zidovudine/nelfinavir/lamiVUDine regimen was associated with increased toxi-
   city (eg, neutropenia) HIV infection, prophylaxis during breastfeeding: Nevirapine is an option for extended post-
   natal prophylaxis of HIV transmission in infants with exposure to HIV during breastfeeding. If
   used, extended prophylaxis should be started at birth or after the completion of initial zidovu-
   dine prophylaxis and continued until 6 weeks after last exposure to breast milk; however, it
   may be reasonable to discontinue prophylaxis earlier when concern for viremia in the breast-
   feeding parent is low Pediatric FDA Approved Indication
