   Preparation
   Extemporaneous oral compounds

   4 mg/mL oral suspension (30mL) 16 , 8
   • Puncture the top of twelve 10-mg NIFEdipine liquid capsules (each capsule contains 34 mL )
   with one needle to create a vent.

   • Insert a second needle into the capsule and use a syringe to extract the liquid.

   • Transfer to a calibrated bottle and add sufficient quantity of a 1:1 mixture of Ora-Plus™ and
   Ora-Sweet SF™ to a total volume of 30 mL. Shake well to mix.
   • Stable at room temperature or under refrigeration for 90 days. Shake well before using.

   4 mg/mL oral suspension (120 mL) 21
   • Weigh out 480 mg NIFEdipine active pharmaceutical ingredient and add to a low-actinic plas-
   tic prescription bottle.

   • Add SyrSpend SF PH4 ® cherry flavored in geometric proportions, mixing well after each
   addition, to a total volume of 120 mL.
   • Shake or stir until a homogenous suspension is achieved.
   • Label the container with "Shake well before using" and "Protect from light."

   • Stable for 92 days under refrigeration (2° to 8°C) or at room temperature.', 'In children, the most common adverse effects associated with the use of calcium channel
   blockers, including NIFEdipine, are headache, flushing, dizziness, tachycardia, gingival hyper-
   plasia, peripheral edema, chest pain, nausea, vomiting, and constipation Oxygen desatura-
   tion was the most commonly reported adverse event in a retrospective study of 1746 doses of
   NIFEdipine administered to 166 pediatric hypertensive patients Monitoring
