   of serotonin, gastrin, vasoactive intestinal peptide, secretin, motilin, and pancreatic polypep-
   tide. After subcutaneous injection, octreotide is absorbed rapidly and completely from the in-
   jection site. Peak reached in approximately 30 minutes, and duration of action is up to 12
   hours. The LAR Depot formulation (IM use) is a long-acting dosage form that releases the drug
   slowly from the injection site, reducing the administration frequency (once every 4 weeks).
