   Olmesartan medoxomil is an angiotensin receptor blocker which blocks the vasoconstrictor
   and aldosterone-secreting effects of angiotensin II by selectively blocking the binding of an-
   giotensin II to the AT1 receptor in many tissues, such as vascular smooth muscle and the
   adrenal gland. Its action is independent of the pathways for angiotensin II synthesis. Does not
   inhibit angiotensin converting enzyme (ACE) and therefore does not affect response to
   bradykinin like ACE inhibitors. Olmesartan medoxomil is a prodrug which is rapidly hydrolyzed
   to olmesartan in the gastrointestinal tract and then rapidly absorbed. Bioavailability is approxi-
   mately 26% and is not affected by food Peak concentrations achieved in approximately 5
   hours in children Highly bound to plasma proteins (99%) and does not penetrate red blood

cells. After initial hydroxylation during absorption, very little further metabolism occurs. Not
   metabolized by cytochrome P450 enzyme system Olmesartan is the only metabolite.
   Eliminated primarily in the feces (60%) and urine (3% to 15%). Clearance increases with in-
   creasing body weight. Elimination half-life in children is approximately 8 to 9 hours'),
