   Elimination

   Following a single dose of 14C-QUEtiapine, less than 1% of the administered dose was ex-
   creted unchanged. Approximately 73% of the QUEtiapine dose was recovered in the urine and
   20% was recovered in the feces 2 ,3 .

   Pediatric patients
   At steady state pharmacokinetics in children and adolescents were similar to adults. When ad-
   justed for dose and weight, the AUC and Cmax of the parent compound were 41% and 39%
   lower, respectively, compared with adults. For the active metabolite, norquetiapine, AUC and
   Cmax were 45% and 31% higher, respectively 2 ,'),
