   Mechanism of action: Inhibits gastric acid secretion by histamine H2-receptor antagonism.
   Oral doses of 6 to 10 mg/kg/day divided every 8 to 12 hours maintain gastric pH greater than 4
   throughout most of the dosing interval. Tmax: Peak serum concentration occurs 2 to 3 hours after oral administration. Absorption is
   rapid after IM administration with mean peak serum concentration occurring within 15 min-
   utes. Bioavailability ranges from 90% to 100% following IM/IV administration and is approxi-
   mately 50% following administration of the tablets. Hepatic biotransformation predominates
   after oral absorption, with 30% excreted unchanged in the urine. In contrast, 70% of an IV dose
   is excreted unchanged in the urine. Elimination half-life in children is similar to that of adults
   which is approximately 2 hours, and is prolonged in patients with renal or hepatic insufficiency
   2 ,25,19
              .

   Pharmacokinetic Studies:

   In children 1 day to 6 years of age (n=17), the half-life, Vd, and Cl were around 4 hours, 2
   L/kg, and 7 mL/min/kg, respectively. In comparison in children older than 12 years of age
   (n=6), the half-life, Vd, and Cl were around 7 hours, 98 L/kg, and 89 mL/min/kg, respec-
   tively In 27 term neonates (mean age, 2 hours), the half-life, Vd, and Cl for raNITIdine
   were 45 hours, 52 L/kg, and 02 mL/kg/min. Single doses of 6 and 3 mg/kg were pre-
   dicted to maintain raNITIdine concentrations greater than 100 and 200 nanograms/mL
   (ng/mL), respectively, for at least 12 hours. Likewise, an infusion rate between 03 and 06
   mg/kg/hr would maintain average steady state concentration in the range of 100 to 200 ng/mL Pharmacodynamic Study
   RaNITIdine versus Famotidine: There was no significant difference in gastric pH between
   famotidine 12 mg/m2 IV and raNITIdine 60 mg/m2 IV at 0, 6, and 12 hours after a single dose
   in 24 critically ill patients 6 months to 16 years of age with a pH of less than 4 at baseline. No
   significant difference between the groups in time for median pH to increase to pH 4, total time
   pH remained above 4, and AUC for pH 5/8'),
