   Solution should be clear after removal from refrigerator; however, the presence of small color-
   less particles is not unusual after refrigeration. Allow solution to reach room temperature and
   gently swirl Do not administer if solution is cloudy 4 , 6 , Injections should be given subQ, directly into the abdomen 13 , thighs or buttocks 3 ,9 or back of
   the upper arm Doses should generally be administered in the evening 13 , 12 ; patients on hemodialysis should
   receive the dose at least 3 to 4 hours after their dialysis session and those on continuous am-
   bulatory peritoneal dialysis should receive the dose after the nighttime exchange. Patients on
   chronic cycling peritoneal dialysis should receive the dose in the morning after dialysis comple-
   tion 5 ,6 .

