   Administration
   Intravenous: Dilute in appropriate volume (as small as 25 mL may be used 2 ) of NS or D5W 31
   to concentrations of 2, 4, or 10 mg/mL 32 and infuse over 20 to 60 minutes Maximum con-
   centration for infusion is 10 mg/mL.

   Intraventricular: When administering via a ventricular drain, clamp the drain for 15 to 60
   minutes to allow the agent to equilibrate throughout the CSF Intramuscular: For the IM route, solution does not need to be further diluted Inhalation solution: Designed to be used with a PARI LC PLUS® reusable nebulizer and either
   a DeVilbiss® Pulmo-Aide® 34 or a PARI Vios® 35 air compressor. Treatment takes approxi-
   mately 15 minutes to complete 35,34 . Tobramycin inhalation therapy is administered after all
   other therapies (eg, chest physiotherapy or other nebulizers) Inhalation powder: Remove capsules from blister pack immediately before use. Capsules are
   designed to be used with a Podhaler™ device for oral inhalation only. Do not swallow the cap-
   sules as the intended effects in the lungs will not be obtained. The Podhaler™ device adminis-
   ters the contents of one tobramycin inhalation capsule at a time. The patient must inhale at
   least twice to obtain the full dose from each capsule. The Podhaler™ device is replaced every 7
   days of tobramycin inhalation powder therapy; always use the new Podhaler™ device provided
   with each weekly pack. Tobramycin inhalation therapy is administered after all other therapies
   (eg, chest physiotherapy or other inhaled medications) 12/23', 'Serious allergic reactions including anaphylaxis and dermatologic reactions (exfoliative der-
