   sputum concentration was 1237 mcg/g (range, 35 to 7414 mcg/g) after 10 minutes and 814
   mcg/g (range, 23 to 2843 mcg/g) after 30 minutes. Three hours after inhalation started, spu-
   tum concentration declined to approximately 15% of those observed at 30 minutes.
   Elimination half-life is approximately 4 hours. Does not accumulate in the sputum. Average
   serum concentration at 1 hour was 95 mcg/mL after inhalation of a single dose, and 05
   mcg/mL after 20 weeks of therapy. Systemically absorbed drug eliminated primarily though
   the kidneys, with unabsorbed drug eliminated in expectorated sputum 35,34 .

