Extemporaneous oral compound

   10 mg/mL suspension (100 mL) 11
   • Empty the contents of ten 100-mg capsules of zonisamide into a mortar and triturate to a
   fine powder.
   • Add a small amount of either a 1:1 mixture of Ora-Plus® and Ora-Sweet® or a 10:1 mixture
   of Simple Syrup NF and 1% methylcellulose to wet the powder and mix into a fine paste.

   • Add chosen vehicle in geometric portions to achieve a final volume of 100 mL, mixing well af-
   ter each addition. Transfer to an appropriately sized plastic prescription bottle.

   • Label the container with "Shake well before using."

   • Stable for 90 days at room temperature (25°C) or under refrigeration (4°C).

   10 mg/mL suspension (300 mL) 12

   • Weigh out 3000 mg of zonisamide active pharmaceutical ingredient and triturate to a fine
   powder using a mortar and pestle.

   • Add a small amount of SyrSpend® SF PH4 to wet the powder and mix into a fine paste.

   • Add SyrSpend® SF PH4 in geometric portions to achieve a final volume of 300 mL, mixing
   well after each addition. Transfer suspension into low-actinic prescription bottles.

   • Label the container with "Shake well before using."

   • Stable for 90 days at room temperature (20 to 25°C) or under refrigeration (2 to 8°C).

   Other extemporaneous oral compounds

   • Simple-syrup suspension: Prepare suspension in a glass mortar. Add enough simple syrup
   85% for a zonisamide concentration of 10 mg/mL. The suspension is stable for at least 28 days
   when stored at room temperature or under refrigeration. Simple syrup can be made with su-
   crose and purified water for a final concentration of 85% (w/w) • Methylcellulose suspension: Prepare suspension in a glass mortar. Add enough methylcel-
   lulose 5% (w/v) for a zonisamide concentration of 10 mg/mL. The suspension is stable for 28
   when stored under refrigeration and for 7 days when stored at room temperature. To make
   methylcellulose 5%, dissolve 5 g of methylcellulose in 300 mL of purified hot water and stir
