  Administration
  Buccal route: Administer buccal tablet immediately after removal from blister pack and within 1 hour of onset of prodromal
  symptoms, before any signs of herpes labialis lesions appear. Apply the round side of the tablet with a dry finger to the upper
  gum just above the incisor tooth (canine fossa) on the side of the mouth with herpes labialis symptoms. To adhere tablet, hold in
  place with slight pressure over the upper lip to 30 seconds. Tablet can be used with food or drink but cannot be crushed,
  chewed, sucked, or swallowed. Patient should not chew gum or brush teeth during administration. Tablet must stay in place for
  at least 6 hours and will gradually dissolve; reposition if needed. If the tablet is swallowed within 6 hours of application, the pa-
  tient should drink a glass of water and reapply a new tablet Intravenous route: Administer as IV infusion over 1 hour at a concentration of 7 mg/mL or less in D5W or NS Ophthalmic: Pull down the lower lid of the affected eye to form a pocket. Apply ointment in the pocket, then close the eye for 1
  to 2 minutes; may wipe away any excess ointment Oral route: take with or without food; for suspension, shake well before measuring each dose Extravasation Management:Although not pediatric-specific, the following are recommendations for extravasation of acidic or
  alkaline, like acyclovir, agents 23 :
   ●   General:
   ●   Stop and disconnect infusion; do not remove the cannula or needle
   ●   Attempt to gently aspirate as much extravasated agent as possible; avoid manual pressure
   ●   Remove cannula or needle
