   Mechanism of action: CloNIDine is a centrally acting alpha-2-adrenergic agonist. Stimulation
   of these alpha-adrenoreceptors in the brain stem results in decreased sympathetic outflow
   from the CNS and in reductions in peripheral resistance, heart rate, and blood pressure. Its ac-
   tion in ADHD is unknown Onset and Peak effect: After oral administration, onset of action of hypotension occurs
   within 30 to 60 minutes with a peak effect within 2 to 4 hours. Peak concentrations occur 3 to 5
   hours after dosing of immediate-release formulation.
