blood with a mean combined penetration ratio of 49 (range, 39 to 58; n=4) Metabolism: Extensive, via CYP2D6 38 , CYP1A2 41,42,38 , and CYP3A4 41,42', 'Pharmacology
   Mechanism of action: cloZAPine is an atypical antipsychotic that antagonizes adrenergic,
   cholinergic, histaminergic, and serotonergic receptors 5 , 13 , In addition to dopamine type 2

(D2) and serotonin type 2 (5-HT2a) receptor antagonism 5 , cloZAPine also interferes weakly
   with dopamine binding at D1, D3, and D5 receptors, and moderately at D4 receptors 13,14 .
   cloZAPine has shown more dopamine blocking activity in the limbic region of the brain
   29 , 30 , 31 , 32
                       than in the neostriatum, but its potency is low in all regions These properties
   may account for the low extrapyramidal side effect profile of cloZAPine 13,14 .

   Time to initial response: 3 months (schizophrenia); in a small number of patients, clinical im-
   provement may be delayed up to 12 months Bioequivalence: cloZAPine oral disintegrating tablets (FazaClo®) and cloZAPine oral suspen-
   sion (Versacloz™) are bioequivalent to cloZAPine tablets 14 , Therapeutic concentration: 350 to 420 mcg/L 35

   Bioavailability: 50% to 60% 30,36,37,38

   Effect of food (orally disintegrating tablet): Cmax decreased by 20% (12.5 mg); Cmin in-
   creased by 21% and Tmax delayed by 5 hours (200 mg) 14

   Effect of food (suspension): Cmax reduced by 20% and Tmax delayed by 5 hours 5

   Effect of food (tablet): No effect 13

   Protein binding: 97% 5 , 13 , 14

   Vd: 6 L/kg 39
   Tissues and Fluids

   • Amniotic fluid: In a systematic review of 49 studies evaluating antipsychotic use during preg-
   nancy and/or breastfeeding, cloZAPine was observed to be present in amniotic fluid with a
   mean combined penetration ratio of 56 (range, 31 to 82; n=3) • Umbilical cord blood: In a systematic review of 49 studies evaluating antipsychotic use during
   pregnancy and/or breastfeeding, cloZAPine was observed to be present in umbilical cord
   blood with a mean combined penetration ratio of 49 (range, 39 to 58; n=4) Metabolism: Extensive, via CYP2D6 38 , CYP1A2 41,42,38 , and CYP3A4 41,42

   Metabolites (active): N-desmethylclozapine (norclozapine) 5 ,13,14

   Renal excretion: 50%; trace amount as unchanged drug 5 , 13 , 14

   Fecal excretion: 30%; trace amount as unchanged drug 5 ,13,14

   Half-life: 8 to 12 hours 5 ,13,14'),
