   Monitoring
   Monitor blood pressure and heart rate. For IV administration, monitor blood pressure at 5 and
   10 minutes after each bolus injection 12 , at 5-minute intervals during continuous infusion, and
   at 15-minute intervals when the infusion is temporarily discontinued. Obtain 2 consistent read-
   ings of blood pressure prior to changing infusion rate In patients on oral therapy, use
   standing blood pressure as an indicator for dose titration after every 2 to 3 days Monitor
   liver function tests periodically 18,20 .', '', 'Pharmacology

Labetalol is an adrenergic receptor blocking agent that possesses blocking activities for both
   selective, competitive, alpha(1)-adrenergic receptors and nonselective, competitive, beta-
   adrenergic receptors Hypotensive effect is within 2 to 5 minutes, peaks at 5 to 15 minutes,
   and lasts 2 to 4 hours following IV administration of a single dose Following oral adminis-
   tration, peak effects occur within 2 to 4 hours with a duration of effect of 8 (100-mg dose) to 12
   (300-mg dose) hours. At steady state, maximum blood pressure response occurs within 24 to
   72 hours Undergoes significant hepatic first-pass metabolism with approximately 85% of la-
   betalol removed during a single passage through the liver. Large interindividual variations in
   bioavailability (10% to 86%) 11 which appears to increase when taken with food. Absolute
   bioavailability of labetalol tablets is 25% due to extensive first-pass metabolism. In hepatically
   impaired patients, bioavailability increases due to decreased first-pass effect. Protein binding
   is approximately 50%. Extensively metabolized in the liver, primarily through conjugation to
   glucuronide metabolites. Approximately 55% to 60% of a dose appears in the urine as conju-
   gates or unchanged drug within the first 24 hours of dosing. Elimination half-life is about 5
   hours and 6 to 8 hours following IV infusion and oral administration, respectively. Not signifi-
   cantly removed by hemodialysis 18,12 .'),
