     resistance

     • Eligibility for shorter regimens: No extensive disease, no extrapulmonary disease except for TB lymphadenopathy, no prior exposure
     to any components of the regimen (exposure = more than 1 month of use)
     • MDR = Multidrug resistant TB, caused by strains resistant to at least both isoniazid and rifampin
     • RR = Rifampin resistant TB; caused by strains resistant to rifampin; may be susceptible or resistant to isoniazid (MDR-TB) or other first
     or second-line drugs
     • MDR/RR TB = caused by strains resistant to at least rifampin (RR) or at least rifampin and isoniazid (MDR)
     • Pre-XDR = caused by strains that meet the definition of MDR TB or RR TB plus are resistant to any fluoroquinolone
     • XDR = Extensively drug resistant TB; caused by strains that meet the definition of MDR/RR TB plus are resistant to any fluoro-
     quinolone and at least 1 additional Group A drug (bedaquiline or linezolid).

