   MetFORMIN 1275 mg daily for 6 months reduced hirsutism and androgen levels in non-obese
   adolescent girls with PCOS having a history of PP who were 3 or more years postmenarche
   (n=10; 13 to 20 years of age). Regular menstrual cycles were reported by all subjects within 4
   months of starting therapy Similar results were seen in a subsequent study of non-obese
   adolescent girls with PCOS and PP born SGA (n=18; mean age 7 years). Menstrual regularity
   was reported in all subjects after 6 months of treatment and ovulation was achieved in 78%.
   Ovulation did not occur in those subjects with the lowest birth weight or most severe hyperan-
   drogenism MetFORMIN 850 mg once daily reduced androgen levels, fat mass, and both insulin levels and
   resistance in a randomized, open-label trial of hyperinsulinemic girls born SGA who presented
   with PP (n=24; 10 to 14 years of age). Reductions in insulin-like growth factor and cholesterol
   levels were also seen A subsequent randomized, open-label study, which included pre-pu-
   bertal (n=33; mean age 8 years) and post-pubertal (n=24; mean age 12 years) girls born SGA
   with PP, metFORMIN produced the same reductions in biochemical markers and body compo-
   sition in both groups, as seen in the previous study. Crossover treatment in the post-pubertal
   group demonstrated reversal of androgen levels, cholesterol, insulin resistance and fat mass
