   Renal Dose Adjustments
   Dosage adjustments are not available for pediatric patients; the following adjustments are indicated
   for adults with a usual dosage of 195 mg (40 to less than 50 kg) or 260 mg (50 kg or greater) orally
   every other week for Opfolda™ or 100 mg 3 times daily for Zavesca®.

   • Renal impairment, mild, Opfolda™: No adjustment necessary 2
   • Renal impairment, mild to moderate, Zavesca®: Starting dose is 100 mg orally twice daily
   (CrCl 50 to 70 mL/min/1.73 m(2) or (CrCl 30 to 50 mL/min/1.73 m(2)) 3
   • Renal impairment, moderate or severe, Opfolda™, 50 kg or greater: 195 mg orally every
   other week (CLcr 15 to 59 mL/minute based on Cockcroft-Gault equation) 2

   • Renal impairment, moderate or severe, Opfolda™, 40 kg to less than 50 kg: 130 mg
   orally every other week 2
   • Renal impairment, severe, Zavesca®: Use not recommended (CrCl less than 30
   mL/min/1.73 m(2)) 3

