   Ribavirin has direct antiviral activity against many RNA viruses, although the mechanism of ac-
   tion has not been fully elucidated. Ribavirin increases the mutation frequency in the genomes
   of several RNA viruses and ribavirin triphosphate inhibits hepatitis C viral polymerase activity.
   Ribavirin is not protein bound. Any involvement of the kidney or liver in ribavirin elimination is
   unknown; however, the 2 pathways of ribavirin metabolism are reversible phosphorylation in
   nucleated cells and degradation by de-ribosylation and amide hydrolysis to the triazole car-
   boxylic acid metabolite. Ribavirin is not a CYP450 enzyme substrate 1 ,4 .
   Oral products: Bioavailability of oral capsules and solution is approximately 60%, with Tmax
