   Pharmacokinetic data are not available for pediatric patients. The following data were ob-
   tained from adult patients. Peak concentrations reached in 2 to 4 hours. Bioavailability is ap-
   proximately 20%; food does not affect absorption. Highly lipophilic drug; protein binding is ap-
   proximately 85%. Metabolized in the liver to five metabolites; the 25-O-desacetyl metabolite
   has activity similar to the parent drug. Substrate for and inducer of CYP3A isoenzymes.
   Excreted in the urine (53%), mainly as metabolites. Fecal elimination accounts for approxi-
   mately 30% of a dose. Mean elimination half-life is 45 hours (range, 16 to 69 hours)'),
