   Autoimmune Hemolytic Anemia; Second-Line
   3 years or older: 375 mg/m2 IV once weekly for 4 weeks. Some patients were retreated up to
   5 times in an observational cohort study (n=61) Granulomatosis with Polyangiitis
   2 years or older

   Induction: 375 mg/m2 IV infusion once weekly for 4 weeks 1
   Induction concomitant medication: MethylPREDNISolone 30 mg/kg (not to exceed 1 g/day)
   IV once daily for 3 days starting prior to the first rituximab infusion, then continue oral steroids
   per clinical practice 1
   Concomitant medication: Give Pneumocystis jiroveci pneumonia prophylaxis during riTUX-
   imab treatment and for at least 6 months following the last riTUXimab infusion 1

   Followup treatment (if disease is controlled following induction and a rituximab product
   was used for induction of active disease): 250 mg/m(2) IV within 24 weeks but no sooner
   than 16 weeks after last rituximab product induction infusion or based on clinical evaluation,
   then 250 mg/m(2) IV 2 weeks later, and 250 mg/m2 IV every 6 months thereafter as clinically
   indicated 1

Followup treatment (if disease is controlled following induction and other standard of
   care immunosuppressants were used for induction of active disease): 250 mg/m(2) IV
   within 4 weeks of active disease control, then 250 mg/m2 IV 2 weeks later, and 250 mg/m(2) IV
   every 6 months thereafter as clinically indicated 1

   Immune Thrombocytopenia (unresponsive to initial treatment and/or persistent or
   chronic):

   1 year or older: 375 mg/m2 IV once weekly for 1 to approximately 6 doses 9 ,10,11 . In one co-
   hort, doses were escalated to 750 mg/m2 IV once weekly for 3 doses if there was no response
   after 3 doses in pediatric patients with hematologic autoimmune cytopenias Juvenile Dermatomyositis, Refractory; Adjunct 5 m2or less Body Surface Area: 575 mg/m2 IV once weekly for 2 doses 12,13 .
   Greater than 5 m2Body Surface Area: 750 mg/m2 IV (MAX 1000 mg/dose) once weekly for
   2 doses 12,13 .

   Juvenile Idiopathic Arthritis, Severe; Refractory

   2 years or older: 375 mg/m2 IV once weekly for 4 doses. Repeat courses may be necessary 6

   Lupus Nephritis

   Refractory or severe: 375 mg/m2 IV every week, for 2 to 4 weeks 14 OR 750 mg/m2 IV per
   dose for 1-2 infusion(s) 2 weeks apart; MAX 1 g/dose 15

   Concomitant medication (glucocortioid): 1 to 2 mg/kg/day orally, MAX dosage 60 mg/day.
   Gradually taper over time. If pulse therapy is desired, administer methylPREDNISolone 30
   mg/kg/dose IV for 3 consecutive days before starting oral glucocorticoid induction therapy,
   MAX 1000 mg/dose 16
   Concomitant medication (DMARD): In refractory cases of Class III/IV with or without Class V,
   riTUXimab should be administered as induction/maintenance treatment with a DMARD (cy-
   closporine, mycophenolate mofetil, azathioprine) 16

   Microscopic Polyangiitis
   2 years or older

   Induction: 375 mg/m2 IV infusion once weekly for 4 weeks 1

