   Prefilled syringe

   • Allow prefilled syringe to sit at room temperature for 30 minutes prior to administration • Inject full amount of prefilled syringe. Patient may self-inject, or a caregiver may administer
   the dose • Rotate injection sites. Do not inject where skin is tender, damaged, bruised or scarred 2/6', 'Common: In a clinical study of 93 pediatric patients with polyarticular juvenile idiopathic
   arthritis (pJIA), the most common adverse effects were nasopharyngitis (36.6%), upper respira-
