   • Allow refrigerated vial to stand for approximately 30 to 60 minutes to reach room tempera-
   ture (20 to 25°C [68 to 77°F]); peel back light protective wrap on vial to inspect the contents in
   the vial, which should be white to almost white broken cake or powdered material. The vial
   needs to be protected from light at all times. Ensure the protective wrap around label is cover-
   ing the entire vial • Reconstitute using a polypropylene syringe with 6 mL of NS and slowly inject into the vial
   with the stream directed toward the inside wall of the vial to obtain a concentration of 225
   mcg/mL of selexipag; complete infusion within 4 hours of first puncture • Gently invert the vial and repeat until powder is completely dissolved; do not shake 5
   • Inspect the vial by peeling back the light protective wrap around label for discoloration. The
   reconstituted solution should appear clear, colorless and free from foreign material. Do not
   use if the reconstituted solution is discolored, cloudy, or contains visible particles • Use glass containers for dilution only 5

   • Withdraw 100 mL of NS and transfer into an empty sterile glass container • Withdraw the required volume of reconstituted solution from the vial using a single, appro-
   priately sized polypropylene syringe and dilute into the glass container containing 100 mL NS
   to obtain the desired final dose • Mix the diluted infusion solution by gentle inversion of the glass container 5 times; do not
