   No specific monitoring has been determined.', '', '• Fecal excretion: 93% 5

   • Total body clearance, 2 to 18 years of age: 9 L/hour 2

   • Total body clearance, adult: 9 L/hour 5

   Elimination Half-Life

   Selexipag: 8 to 5 hours 5

   Active metabolite: 2 to 5 hours 5

   Population Pharmacokinetics
   Pediatric dosing was obtained using an adult pharmacokinetic model, as age-related metabo-
   lism and clearance differences of selexipag were not expected between the populations. The
   initial doses were to provide an expected AUC similar to that in adults taking 200 mcg twice
   daily, with titration up to 1600 mcg twice daily. For pediatric patients, doses derived from the
   model were 100 mcg twice daily (titrated to maximum of 800 mcg twice daily) for those 9 to
   less than 25 kg; 150 mcg twice daily (titrated to maximum of 1200 mcg twice daily) for those 25
   to less than 50 kg; and 200 mcg twice daily (titrated to maximum of 1600 mcg twice daily) for
   those 50 kg or greater. These dosages were then studied in 62 pediatric patients 2 years or
   older. AUC was not significantly different from that of adults among any age, weight or dose
   group, and there were no apparent differences based on administration (whole tablet, taking
   with soft food, or dispersing tablet in apple or orange juice)'),
