   target trough blood levels vary, depending on transplant type, time since transplantation, con-
   comitant immunosuppressants, and specific transplant center protocols 16,13,22,9 ,3 ,18,25,21 .
   • Levels obtained by chromatographic and immunoassay methodologies are not interchange-
   able. Effective monitoring requires knowledge of which assay is being used, any change to the
   assay used, and any change to the laboratory''s reference range Renal Transplant Rejection Prophylaxis
   • Monitor trough levels at least 3 to 4 days after initiation of therapy using a loading dose, and
