      or carbapenem as empiric therapy (1A).

      Reserve addition of a second Gram-negative agent or a glycopeptide for patients who are
      clinically unstable, when a resistant infection is suspected, or in centers with a high rate of
      resistant pathogens (1B).

      Low-Risk FN
      Consider initial or step-down outpatient management if infrastructure is in place to en-
      sure careful monitoring and follow-up (2B).

      Consider oral antibiotic administration if child able to tolerate route reliably (2B).

      Ongoing Management of FN: 24 to 72 hours or more after initiation of empiric antibacte-
      rial treatment

