   Renal and Hepatic Dose Adjustments
   Renal impairment

   • Injection, GFR 10 to 50 mL/min: Administer 75% of the normal fentanyl dose • Injection, GFR less than 10 mL/min: Administer 50% of the normal fentanyl dose • Oral transmucosal: Use with caution • Transdermal: With mild to moderate renal impairment, start with one-half of the usual
   transdermal dose. Avoid use in patients with severe renal impairment Hepatic impairment

   • Transdermal: With mild to moderate hepatic impairment, start with one-half of the usual
   transdermal dose. Avoid use in patients with severe hepatic impairment • Transmucosal: Use with caution 5/29
Other Dose Adjustments

   Extracorporeal membrane oxygenation (ECMO): FentaNYL is highly extracted by the ECMO
   circuit, resulting in an increase in volume of distribution and a need for dose increases over
   time. The high extraction rate is likely due to the high lipophilicity of fentaNYL and its affinity
   for membrane oxygenators and roller-head pumps. Consider a larger initial loading dose if
   opting to use fentaNYL or consider an alternative medication 50,51 .', 'Injection 79

