   chest pain, pulmonary congestion, rhinitis, skin necrosis, tachycardia, thirst, thrombophlebitis,
   urinary retention, urticaria, and blurred vision Black Box Warning
   Inhalation
   Mannitol acts as a bronchoconstrictor and may cause severe bronchospasm. Mannitol
   bronchial challenge testing is for diagnostic purposes only and should be conducted only by
   trained professionals under the supervision of a physician familiar with the test and manage-
   ment of acute bronchospasm (ie, testing area equipped with appropriate medications and
   equipment). Immediately administer a short-acting inhaled beta-agonist in the event of severe
   bronchospasm. Do not perform bronchial challenge testing with mannitol in a patient with
   asthma or very low baseline pulmonary function tests (eg, FEV1 less than 1 to 5 L or less than
   70% of the predicted values) Terminal Injection Site Compatibility
