   Pediatric Approved Indications

   Indicated for the treatment of anemia associated with chronic kidney disease in adults on dial-
   ysis and not on dialysis, and pediatric patients aged 3 months to 17 years on dialysis or not on
   dialysis who are converting from another erythropoiesis-stimulating agent (ESA) after their he-
   moglobin level was stabilized with an ESA 2

   Limitations of Use

   • Methoxy polyethylene glycol-epoetin beta is not indicated or recommended in the treatment
   of anemia due to cancer chemotherapy 4/10
• Methoxy polyethylene glycol-epoetin beta is not indicated or recommended as a substitute
   for RBC transfusions in patients who require immediate correction of anemia • Methoxy polyethylene glycol-epoetin beta has not demonstrated improvement in symptoms,
   physical function, or health-related quality of life 1

   Administration
   • Administer IV or subQ 2

   • IV is the preferred route in patients receiving hemodialysis • Do not mix with any parenteral solution • In patients less than 6 years, maintain the same route of administration as the previous ESA
